<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "pwm.fan.control">
<!ENTITY author    "IDmedia">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.11.23">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IDmedia/pwm-fan-control/main/pwm.fan.control.plg">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" min="7.4.0" support="https://github.com/IDmedia/pwm-fan-control/issues" icon="icon-fan" launch="Settings/PWMFanControl">

<CHANGES>
###2026.11.23
- Notifications show which server they come from: the title is "PWM Fan Control - &lt;server&gt;" and the subject starts with "[&lt;SERVER&gt;]", like Unraid's own notifications
- Fixed: when spun-down disks spin up, Unraid can take several minutes to show their temperature. This no longer counts as a fan problem: for up to 10 minutes the fans run at the lowest speed of the curve (at least the spun-down speed), then at full speed with an alert as before
- "Problem resolved" notifications say the problem is gone instead of only repeating its text

###2026.11.18
- The group editor only offers named fans (and the fans already in the group). Unnamed outputs, usually empty headers, are behind a "Show unnamed outputs" link
- A fan that gets a name shows up in the group editor right away

###2026.11.17b
- Disk temperatures are now separate sources: Array (parity and data disks), one per pool, Unassigned disks and Flash, so HDD, SSD and NVMe pools can have their own curves
- Existing groups get the Array source and a source for every pool that was monitored, with the curve of the former Array disks source, so nothing changes until you edit the curves
- The "Disk types to monitor" setting is gone: add the disk sources you want to a group instead. Single disks can still be unticked
- Identify without a paired RPM sensor ignores other fans on the same chip that change speed during the test

###2026.11.17a
- Fixed: fans at full speed on nct6775 chips were reported as "changed by something else" (the driver shows manual mode at 100% as mode 0)
- When a fan's speed keeps being changed by something else, the syslog says what was set and found, and whether the mode changed (BIOS) or only the speed (another program)

###2026.11.17
- Requires Unraid 7.4 or newer
- Fan icon from Unraid's own icon set instead of the snowflake
- Speed changes are no longer logged to syslog by default, problems still are
- Speed test: steps a fan down from 100% until it stops, then finds the speed it needs to start again; the fan stands still only for a few seconds at a time
- Fan tests don't start, and stop right away, when the fan's group needs it (temperature at or above high, source unreadable, parity check)
- Identify slows fans to 20% by default instead of stopping them, and keeps them slow until they have stopped slowing down (8 seconds per step by default)
- Warns when a group's min speed is below the speed one of its fans needs to start
- Warns when a fan stops spinning (0 RPM) while it should run, and when another program changes a fan's speed
- Problems are sent as Unraid alert notifications when they last more than a minute, a crash or watchdog restart right away, and a notice when resolved
- Notifications don't flood: one alert per problem, resolved only after 2 minutes without it, the same problem at most every 4 hours, no repeat after a service restart, crash and watchdog alerts at most once an hour
- A temperature source that can't be read or is gone (e.g. Nvidia driver missing after an update) now shows a warning and sends an alert; before, its fans silently ran at full speed
- A stopped array counts as spun down instead of unreadable
- No alerts in the first 5 minutes after boot, while drivers load and the array starts
- Warns when a fan runs much faster or slower than its speed test measured, which usually means fans were moved to other headers
- Missing fans say why: the chip is gone (driver not loaded, ACPI conflict) or only that output (hardware or BIOS changed)
- Hardware check on the settings page: fan driver, fan outputs, ACPI resource conflicts and whether acpi_enforce_resources=lax is needed
- New setting "Drivers to load": loads the fan controller driver (with options) at boot
- Points out fans in a group without a paired RPM sensor, which can't be watched
- A single failed temperature reading no longer sends fans to full speed; two in a row still do
- An error in the service, or a crash, now runs the fans at full speed instead of leaving them at their last speed
- Disk temperature sensors of the kernel (drivetemp) are no longer read, so disks can spin down
- Dashboard tile uses a lighter request and shows warnings
- Shows when a fan header is in DC mode
- Settings and fan names are only written to the flash drive when they change

###2026.11.16
- First release of PWM Fan Control, replacing the unreleased Array Fan Control plugin
- Fan groups: every group follows one or more temperature sources, the highest speed wins
- Temperature sources: array disks, Nvidia GPUs (nvidia-smi) and kernel sensors (CPU, motherboard, NVMe)
- Background service checking every 2-30 seconds, with a watchdog and a slow-down delay
- Runs at full speed when a temperature can't be read
- Identify fans from the web UI with live RPM readings, name fans and sensors
- Fan curve and 24 hour history charts per group, dashboard tile
- Imports settings from Array Fan Control
</CHANGES>

<!-- Remove files from a previous version -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/pwm.fan.control
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/PWMFanControl.page">
<INLINE><![CDATA[Menu="Utilities"
Title="PWM Fan Control"
Icon="icon-fan"
Tag="icon-fan"
Markdown="false"
---
<?php
$pfc_dir = '/plugins/pwm.fan.control';
$pfc_csrf = $var['csrf_token'] ?? (@parse_ini_file('/var/local/emhttp/var.ini')['csrf_token'] ?? '');
$pfc_v = @filemtime("/usr/local/emhttp$pfc_dir/js/pfc.js");
?>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<?=$pfc_dir?>/css/pfc.css?v=<?=$pfc_v?>">

<div id="pfc" data-api="<?=$pfc_dir?>/include/api.php" data-csrf="<?=htmlspecialchars($pfc_csrf)?>">

  <div id="pfc-banners"></div>

  <div class="pfc-applybar pfc-hidden" id="pfc-applybar">
    <span><i class="fa fa-pencil"></i> You have unsaved changes.</span>
    <button type="button" class="pfc-apply">Apply</button>
    <button type="button" class="pfc-reset">Discard</button>
  </div>

  <!-- Status -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-tachometer title"></i>Status</span></div>
  <div class="pfc-status" id="pfc-status"></div>

  <!-- Groups -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-object-group title"></i>Fan groups</span></div>
  <p class="pfc-muted">
    A group is a set of fans that follow one or more temperature sources. Every source has its own curve, and the group
    runs at the <b>highest speed any of its sources asks for</b>. Fans speed up right away and slow down only after the
    lower speed has been needed for the <b>slow-down delay</b>. If a source can't be read, the group runs at full speed.
  </p>
  <div id="pfc-groups"></div>
  <p><button type="button" id="pfc-add-group"><i class="fa fa-plus"></i> Add group</button></p>

  <!-- Fans -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="icon-fan title"></i>Fans</span></div>
  <p class="pfc-muted">
    Click <b>Identify</b> to slow a fan down and spin it up to full speed, then watch or listen to see which fan reacts.
    The RPM sensor that reacts is paired with the output automatically. Give each fan a name, then add it to a group above.
    <b>Speed test</b> steps the fan down from 100% until it stops, and shows the speed a fan stops at and the speed it needs to
    start again. The fan stands still only for a few seconds at a time. With a paired RPM sensor, a fan that stops spinning while
    it should run is reported, and after a speed test also a fan that runs much faster or slower than measured, which usually
    means fans were moved to other headers.
    During a test the fan doesn't follow its group, so a test doesn't start, and stops right away, when the group needs the fan:
    a temperature at or above its <b>high</b> setting, a source that can't be read, or a parity check.
  </p>
  <div class="pfc-table-wrap">
    <table class="pfc-table" id="pfc-pwm-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Output</th><th>Speed</th><th>Current setting</th><th>RPM sensor</th><th>Group</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><td colspan="7" class="pfc-muted">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div id="pfc-fantest" class="pfc-fantest pfc-hidden"></div>

  <div id="pfc-rpm-section" class="pfc-hidden">
    <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-circle-o-notch title"></i>Other fan sensors</span></div>
    <p class="pfc-muted">RPM sensors that are not paired with a controllable output, e.g. fans on headers without PWM control. You can still give them a name.</p>
    <div class="pfc-table-wrap">
      <table class="pfc-table" id="pfc-rpm-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Sensor</th><th>Speed</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Sources -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-thermometer-half title"></i>Temperature sources</span></div>
  <p class="pfc-muted">Everything that reports a temperature. Give sources a name to recognise them in groups and charts.
    <span id="pfc-nvidia-note"></span></p>
  <div class="pfc-table-wrap">
    <table class="pfc-table" id="pfc-source-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Source</th><th>Temperature</th><th>Used by</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <label class="pfc-muted"><input type="checkbox" id="pfc-show-all-sensors"> Show all kernel sensors</label>

  <!-- Disks -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-hdd-o title"></i>Disks</span></div>
  <p class="pfc-muted">Disk temperatures come as one source per part of the server: <b>Array</b> (parity and data disks), one
    <b>Pool</b> source for every pool, <b>Unassigned disks</b> and <b>Flash</b>. Each reports the hottest of its disks that is
    spun up, so HDDs, SSDs and NVMe drives in different pools can have their own curve. Untick a disk to ignore it, e.g. a disk
    that runs hot but isn't cooled by these fans. Unraid only refreshes disk temperatures every 30 minutes by default. You can
    lower this under Settings &gt; Disk Settings &gt; Tunable (poll_attributes).</p>
  <div class="pfc-table-wrap">
    <table class="pfc-table" id="pfc-disk-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Disk</th><th>Source</th><th>State</th><th>Temperature</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <form class="pfc-form" onsubmit="return false">
    <dl><dt>Full speed during parity check:</dt><dd>
      <select data-cfg="array.parity_full_speed" data-type="bool"><option value="true">Yes</option><option value="false">No</option></select>
      <span class="pfc-muted">Applies to the Array source.</span>
    </dd></dl>
  </form>

  <!-- Settings -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-cog title"></i>Settings</span></div>
  <form class="pfc-form" onsubmit="return false">
    <dl><dt>Enable fan control:</dt><dd>
      <select data-cfg="enabled" data-type="bool"><option value="false">No</option><option value="true">Yes</option></select>
      <span class="pfc-muted">While disabled, the plugin never changes any fan speed.</span>
    </dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Check temperatures every:</dt><dd>
      <select data-cfg="interval" data-type="int">
        <option value="2">2 seconds</option><option value="3">3 seconds</option><option value="5">5 seconds</option>
        <option value="10">10 seconds</option><option value="15">15 seconds</option><option value="30">30 seconds</option>
      </select>
    </dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Log speed changes to syslog:</dt><dd>
      <select data-cfg="log_changes" data-type="bool"><option value="false">No</option><option value="true">Yes</option></select>
      <span class="pfc-muted">Changes of 5% or more, and every switch to or from full speed. Useful while tuning curves. Problems are always logged.</span>
    </dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Send notifications:</dt><dd>
      <select data-cfg="notify" data-type="bool"><option value="true">Yes</option><option value="false">No</option></select>
      <span class="pfc-muted">An Unraid alert when a problem lasts more than a minute (a fan stopped or was moved, a fan or source is missing,
        the service failed, ...) and a notice when it is resolved.</span>
    </dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Drivers to load:</dt><dd>
      <input type="text" class="pfc-wide" data-cfg="drivers" maxlength="200" placeholder="e.g. nct6775">
      <span class="pfc-muted">Fan controller drivers loaded at boot, before fan control starts. Separate several with ";", options are allowed
        (e.g. "it87 force_id=0x8628"). Leave empty if another plugin (e.g. Dynamix System Temperature) loads the driver.</span>
    </dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Identify: slow speed:</dt><dd><input type="number" min="0" max="100" class="pfc-narrow" data-cfg="identify.low_pwm" data-type="pct"> % <span class="pfc-muted">Default 20%: clearly slower, without stopping the fan. 0% stops most fans.</span></dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Identify: seconds per step:</dt><dd><input type="number" min="3" max="30" class="pfc-narrow" data-cfg="identify.seconds" data-type="int"> <span class="pfc-muted">The slow step goes on until the fan has stopped slowing down, at most 30 seconds.</span></dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>&nbsp;</dt><dd>
      <button type="button" class="pfc-apply">Apply</button>
      <button type="button" class="pfc-reset">Discard</button>
    </dd></dl>
  </form>

  <!-- Hardware check -->
  <div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-stethoscope title"></i>Hardware check</span></div>
  <p class="pfc-muted">What fan control needs from the system. <b>acpi_enforce_resources=lax</b> is only needed when the kernel log shows an
    ACPI resource conflict for the fan chip: then the BIOS claims the chip and the driver can't load or offers no fan outputs.</p>
  <div class="pfc-table-wrap">
    <table class="pfc-table" id="pfc-hw-table"><tbody></tbody></table>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="<?=$pfc_dir?>/js/pfc.js?v=<?=$pfc_v?>"></script>
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/PWMFanControlDashboard.page">
<INLINE><![CDATA[Menu="Dashboard:0"
---
<?php
$pluginname = 'pwm.fan.control';
$mytiles[$pluginname]['column2'] = <<<'EOT'
<tbody id="pfc-tile" title="PWM Fan Control">
<tr><td>
<i class="icon-fan f32"></i>
<div class="section">PWM Fan Control<br>
<span id="pfc-tile-status">Loading...</span></div>
<a href="/Settings/PWMFanControl" title="Fan settings"><i class="fa fa-fw fa-cog control"></i></a>
</td></tr>
<tr><td>
<div id="pfc-tile-groups" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 18px;padding:2px 0 8px"></div>
<div id="pfc-tile-fans" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(140px,1fr));gap:10px 16px;padding:4px 0"></div>
</td></tr>
<script>
(function () {
  var API = '/plugins/pwm.fan.control/include/api.php';
  function esc(s) { return String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, function (c) { return { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;' }[c]; }); }
  function update() {
    $.getJSON(API, { action: 'tile' }).done(function (s) {
      var live = s.status;
      var warnings = live ? live.warnings.length : 0;
      $('#pfc-tile-status').html(live
        ? 'Running' + (warnings ? ' · <a href="/Settings/PWMFanControl" style="color:#d9534f" title="' + esc(live.warnings.join('\n')) + '">' + warnings + ' warning' + (warnings === 1 ? '' : 's') + '</a>' : '')
        : (s.enabled ? '<span style="color:#d9534f">Not running</span>' : 'Fan control disabled'));

      // Groups: name, speed and what drives it
      var names = {};
      s.groups.forEach(function (g) { names[g.id] = g.name; });
      $('#pfc-tile-groups').html(s.groups.map(function (g) {
        var st = live && live.groups[g.id];
        return st ? '<div title="' + esc(st.reason) + '"><b>' + esc(g.name) + '</b> ' + st.percent + '%</div>' : '';
      }).join(''));

      // One entry per RPM sensor, named after its fan output when paired
      var pairedBy = {}, owner = {};
      s.pwm.forEach(function (p) {
        if (p.rpm_key && p.rpm_key !== 'none') pairedBy[p.rpm_key] = p;
        if (p.group) owner[p.key] = names[p.group];
      });
      var items = [];
      s.rpm.forEach(function (r) {
        var p = pairedBy[r.key];
        var name = (p && p.label) || r.label || r.driver_label || ('Fan ' + r.index);
        if (!r.rpm && !(p && p.label) && !r.label) return; // hide empty, unnamed headers
        var extra = p && p.value != null ? ' · ' + Math.round(p.value * 100 / 255) + '%' : '';
        var icon = p && owner[p.key] ? ' <i class="icon-fan" title="Controlled by ' + esc(owner[p.key]) + '"></i>' : '';
        items.push('<div><div>' + esc(name) + icon + '</div><div style="opacity:.75">' + (r.rpm == null ? 'n/a' : r.rpm + ' RPM') + esc(extra) + '</div></div>');
      });
      $('#pfc-tile-fans').html(items.length ? items.join('') : '<div style="opacity:.75">No fans found</div>');
    });
  }
  update();
  setInterval(update, 5000);
})();
</script>
</tbody>
EOT;
?>
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/README.md">
<INLINE><![CDATA[**PWM Fan Control**

Controls motherboard PWM fans based on temperatures: array disks, Nvidia GPUs, CPU and other sensors. Identify which header drives which fan, name your fans, group them, and give every temperature source its own fan curve. Settings are under Settings > Utilities > PWM Fan Control.
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/css/pfc.css">
<INLINE><![CDATA[/* PWM Fan Control - uses currentColor so it follows every Unraid theme */
#pfc { --pfc-accent: #f0820a; --pfc-error: #d9534f; --pfc-ok: #3c9a4d; --pfc-info: #3b82f6; }
#pfc .pfc-hidden { display: none !important; }
#pfc .pfc-muted { opacity: .65; }
#pfc .pfc-small { font-size: .85em; }
#pfc .pfc-narrow { width: 70px; }
#pfc .pfc-wide { width: 260px; max-width: 100%; }
#pfc .pfc-ok-text { color: var(--pfc-ok); }
#pfc .pfc-log { font-family: monospace; font-size: .85em; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }
#pfc .pfc-error-text { color: var(--pfc-error); }

#pfc .pfc-banner { margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 4px solid var(--pfc-error); background: rgba(217, 83, 79, .1); }
#pfc .pfc-banner-warn { border-color: var(--pfc-accent); background: rgba(240, 130, 10, .1); }
#pfc .pfc-banner-info { border-color: var(--pfc-info); background: rgba(59, 130, 246, .1); }

#pfc .pfc-applybar {
  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 20; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin: 10px 0; padding: 8px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--pfc-accent); border-radius: 4px;
  background: var(--pfc-bar-bg, rgba(240, 130, 10, .15)); backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
}
#pfc .pfc-applybar span { margin-right: auto; }
#pfc .pfc-applybar button { margin: 0; }

#pfc .pfc-status { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin: 12px 0 18px; }
#pfc .pfc-stat {
  flex: 1 1 200px; padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, .3); border-radius: 4px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;
}
#pfc .pfc-stat-label { font-size: .85em; opacity: .65; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em; }
#pfc .pfc-stat-value { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: bold; }

#pfc .pfc-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
#pfc .pfc-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 6px 0 12px; }
#pfc .pfc-table th { text-align: left; font-weight: normal; opacity: .65; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, .35); white-space: nowrap; }
#pfc .pfc-table td { padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, .15); vertical-align: middle; }
#pfc .pfc-table input[type=text] { width: 100%; min-width: 140px; max-width: 240px; margin: 0; }
#pfc .pfc-table input[type=number] { margin: 0; }
#pfc .pfc-table select, #pfc .pfc-table button { margin: 0; }
#pfc .pfc-active-row td { background: rgba(240, 130, 10, .12); }
#pfc .pfc-dim td { opacity: .5; }
#pfc .pfc-hot { color: var(--pfc-error); }
#pfc .pfc-icon-btn { min-width: 0; padding: 4px 8px; }

#pfc .pfc-group { margin: 12px 0 22px; padding: 12px 16px; border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, .35); border-radius: 6px; }
#pfc .pfc-group-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
#pfc .pfc-group-head .pfc-g-name { font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: bold; width: 240px; margin: 0; }
#pfc .pfc-group-head label { white-space: nowrap; }
#pfc .pfc-group-head .pfc-g-delete { margin: 0 0 0 auto; }
#pfc .pfc-group-section { margin-top: 12px; }
#pfc .pfc-group-label { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 6px; }
#pfc .pfc-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
#pfc .pfc-chip { padding: 4px 10px; border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, .4); border-radius: 14px; cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
#pfc .pfc-chip input { margin: 0 4px 0 0; vertical-align: middle; }
#pfc .pfc-chip-on { border-color: var(--pfc-accent); background: rgba(240, 130, 10, .12); }
#pfc .pfc-chip-off { opacity: .5; cursor: default; }
#pfc .pfc-bind-table { max-width: 1000px; }
#pfc .pfc-swatch { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 8px; vertical-align: middle; }
#pfc .pfc-swatch-lg { width: 6px; height: 28px; margin: 0; }
#pfc .pfc-g-addsrc { margin: 0; max-width: 100%; }

#pfc .pfc-fantest { margin: 0 0 18px; padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--pfc-accent); border-radius: 4px; }
#pfc .pfc-fantest-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
#pfc .pfc-fantest-head button { margin: 0 0 0 auto; }
#pfc .pfc-progress { height: 6px; margin: 10px 0; background: rgba(128, 128, 128, .2); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden; }
#pfc .pfc-progress div { height: 100%; background: var(--pfc-accent); transition: width .9s linear; }
#pfc .pfc-fantest-table { max-width: 720px; }
#pfc .pfc-reacted td { color: var(--pfc-ok); font-weight: bold; }

#pfc .pfc-charts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px; margin-top: 12px; }
#pfc .pfc-chart-box { flex: 1 1 380px; min-width: 0; }
#pfc .pfc-chart-title { margin-bottom: 4px; }
#pfc .pfc-chart { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
#pfc .pfc-grid { stroke: currentColor; stroke-opacity: .12; }
#pfc .pfc-axis { fill: currentColor; fill-opacity: .65; font-size: 11px; }
#pfc .pfc-line { fill: none; stroke-width: 2.5; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
#pfc .pfc-line-thin { stroke-width: 1.6; }
#pfc .pfc-line-fan { stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 2.5; }
#pfc .pfc-now { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 2; }
#pfc .pfc-legend { font-size: .9em; opacity: .8; margin-top: 4px; }
#pfc .pfc-key { display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 3px; margin: 0 4px 3px 0; vertical-align: middle; }
#pfc .pfc-key-fan { background: currentColor; }
#pfc .pfc-checks label { margin-right: 14px; white-space: nowrap; }
#pfc .pfc-nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
#pfc .pfc-nowrap button + button { margin-left: 6px; }
#pfc .pfc-warn-text { color: var(--pfc-accent); }
#pfc .pfc-warn-text:empty { display: none; }
#pfc .pfc-fantest-body { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px; align-items: flex-start; }
#pfc .pfc-fantest-body .pfc-fantest-table { flex: 1 1 380px; }
#pfc .pfc-speed-chart { flex: 1 1 380px; max-width: 560px; }
#pfc .pfc-marker { stroke: var(--pfc-accent); stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }
#pfc .pfc-toggle-unnamed { align-self: center; margin-left: 4px; }
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/api.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - AJAX endpoint for the settings page and dashboard tile.
 * GET  ?action=state[&history=1]          everything the settings page shows
 * GET  ?action=tile                       what the dashboard tile shows (cheap: no nvidia-smi, no disks)
 * POST action=save_config, config=<json>  settings and fan groups
 * POST action=save_fan                    name / paired RPM sensor of a PWM output
 * POST action=save_rpm_label              name of an RPM sensor
 * POST action=save_source_label           name of a temperature source
 * POST action=fantest, key=..., mode=identify|speed
 * POST action=fantest_stop                stop the test and restore the fan
 * (POST requests are protected by Unraid's csrf_token check.)
 */
require_once __DIR__ . '/common.php';

header('Content-Type: application/json');

function pfc_reply(array $data, int $code = 200): void {
    http_response_code($code);
    echo json_encode($data, JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES | JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE);
    exit;
}

function pfc_fail(string $msg, int $code = 400): void {
    pfc_reply(['ok' => false, 'error' => $msg], $code);
}

/** The service status, only while the service is actually running. */
function pfc_live_status(): ?array {
    $pid = pfc_daemon_pid();
    $status = $pid ? pfc_read_json(PFC_STATUS) : null;
    return is_array($status) ? $status : null;
}

$migrated = pfc_migrate_old();
$action = $_POST['action'] ?? $_GET['action'] ?? 'state';

switch ($action) {

case 'state':
    $cfg = pfc_load_config();
    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
    $disks = pfc_read_disks($cfg);
    $nv = pfc_nvidia();
    $sources = pfc_read_sources($cfg, $hw, $fans, $disks, $nv);
    $status = pfc_live_status();

    // Disks that just spun up: only the service knows how long they have been waiting for a temperature
    foreach ($status['sources'] ?? [] as $id => $s) {
        if (($s['state'] ?? '') === 'waiting' && !empty($sources[$id]['no_temp'])) {
            $sources[$id]['state'] = 'waiting';
            $sources[$id]['detail'] = $s['detail'];
        }
    }

    // Groups as they would run right now, without the slow-down delay
    $preview = [];
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) $preview[$g['id']] = pfc_group_demand($g, $sources);

    pfc_reply([
        'ok'         => true,
        'time'       => time(),
        'config'     => $cfg,
        'errors'     => pfc_validate_config($cfg),
        'running'    => pfc_daemon_pid() !== null,
        'status'     => $status,
        'pwm'        => pfc_fan_list($cfg, $fans, $hw),
        'hardware'   => ($check = pfc_hardware_check($hw)) + ['hint' => pfc_hardware_hint($check)],
        'rpm'        => pfc_rpm_list($fans, $hw),
        'sources'    => array_values($sources),
        'disks'      => $disks,
        'nvidia'     => ['available' => $nv['available'], 'error' => $nv['error']],
        'preview'    => $preview,
        'history'    => isset($_GET['history']) ? pfc_read_json(PFC_HISTORY, []) : null,
        'fantest'    => pfc_read_json(PFC_FANTEST),
        'old_plugin' => is_dir(PFC_OLD_PLUGIN),
        'migrated'   => $migrated,
    ]);

case 'tile':
    $cfg = pfc_load_config();
    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
    pfc_reply([
        'ok'      => true,
        'enabled' => $cfg['enabled'],
        'groups'  => array_map(fn($g) => ['id' => $g['id'], 'name' => $g['name']], $cfg['groups']),
        'status'  => pfc_live_status(),
        'pwm'     => array_map(fn($p) => array_intersect_key($p, array_flip(['key', 'label', 'rpm_key', 'value', 'group'])), pfc_fan_list($cfg, $fans, $hw)),
        'rpm'     => pfc_rpm_list($fans, $hw),
    ]);

case 'save_config':
    $raw = json_decode((string)($_POST['config'] ?? ''), true);
    if (!is_array($raw)) pfc_fail('Invalid data.');
    $cfg = pfc_normalize_config($raw);
    $errors = pfc_validate_config($cfg);
    if ($errors) pfc_fail(implode("\n", $errors));
    if ($cfg['enabled'] && is_dir(PFC_OLD_PLUGIN)) {
        pfc_fail('Remove the old "Array Fan Control" plugin first, otherwise both plugins will fight over the fans.');
    }
    // Only known fans can be added to a group (fans already in a group may be missing right now)
    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
    $known = pfc_controlled_keys(pfc_load_config());
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) foreach ($g['fans'] as $key) {
        if (!isset($hw['pwm'][$key]) && !isset($known[$key])) pfc_fail("Unknown fan: $key");
    }
    if (!pfc_save_config($cfg)) pfc_fail('Could not write the settings to the flash drive.', 500);
    pfc_apply_service($cfg);
    pfc_reply(['ok' => true, 'running' => pfc_daemon_pid() !== null]);

case 'save_fan':
    $key = (string)($_POST['key'] ?? '');
    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
    if (!isset($hw['pwm'][$key]) && !isset($fans['pwm'][$key])) pfc_fail('Unknown fan.');
    $f = $fans['pwm'][$key] ?? [];
    if (isset($_POST['label'])) $f['label'] = pfc_clean_label($_POST['label']);
    if (isset($_POST['rpm'])) {
        $rpm = (string)$_POST['rpm'];
        if ($rpm !== '' && $rpm !== 'none' && !isset($hw['rpm'][$rpm])) pfc_fail('Unknown RPM sensor.');
        if ($rpm === '') unset($f['rpm']);
        else $f['rpm'] = $rpm;
        // A speed test measured with another sensor no longer applies
        if (isset($f['test']['rpm_key']) && $f['test']['rpm_key'] !== $rpm) unset($f['test']);
    }
    $fans['pwm'][$key] = $f;
    if (!pfc_save_fans($fans)) pfc_fail('Could not write to the flash drive.', 500);
    pfc_reply(['ok' => true]);

case 'save_rpm_label':
case 'save_source_label':
    $key = (string)($_POST['key'] ?? '');
    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
    if ($action === 'save_rpm_label') {
        if (!isset(pfc_scan_hwmon()['rpm'][$key])) pfc_fail('Unknown RPM sensor.');
        $section = 'rpm';
    } else {
        if (!preg_match('/^(array|nvidia:GPU-[\w-]+|hwmon:\S+\/temp\d+)$/', $key)) pfc_fail('Unknown temperature source.');
        $section = 'temp';
    }
    $label = pfc_clean_label($_POST['label'] ?? '');
    if ($label === '') unset($fans[$section][$key]);
    else $fans[$section][$key] = ['label' => $label];
    if (!pfc_save_fans($fans)) pfc_fail('Could not write to the flash drive.', 500);
    pfc_reply(['ok' => true]);

case 'fantest':
    $key = (string)($_POST['key'] ?? '');
    $mode = (string)($_POST['mode'] ?? 'identify');
    if (!in_array($mode, ['identify', 'speed'], true)) pfc_fail('Unknown test.');
    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
    if (!isset($hw['pwm'][$key])) pfc_fail('Unknown fan.');
    if (!$hw['pwm'][$key]['writable']) pfc_fail('This PWM output is not writable.');
    $needed = pfc_fan_needed(pfc_load_config(), $key, $hw);
    if ($needed) pfc_fail("Not started, the fan is needed right now: $needed. Try again when it is cooler.");
    $error = pfc_fantest_start($key, $mode);
    if ($error) pfc_fail($error);
    pfc_reply(['ok' => true]);

case 'fantest_stop':
    @mkdir(PFC_RUN, 0777, true);
    touch(PFC_STOP_FLAG);
    pfc_reply(['ok' => true]);

default:
    pfc_fail('Unknown action.');
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/common.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - shared code for the web UI, API, service and scripts.
 *
 * Concepts
 *   Fan     A PWM output on a motherboard/controller chip ("<chip>@<device>/pwmN"). Keys use the chip name
 *           instead of /sys/class/hwmon/hwmonX, because the hwmonX number can change between boots.
 *   Source  Something that reports a temperature:
 *             "array"                  hottest used, spun-up parity or data disk
 *             "pool:<name>"            the same for one pool; "unassigned" and "flash" for the others
 *             "nvidia:<GPU uuid>"      an Nvidia GPU (via nvidia-smi)
 *             "hwmon:<chip>/tempN"     any kernel temperature sensor (CPU, motherboard, NVMe, ...)
 *   Group   A set of fans following one or more sources. Every source has its own curve and the
 *           group runs at the highest speed any of its sources asks for.
 *
 * Files
 *   config.php    settings and fan groups (config.json)
 *   hardware.php  hwmon scan, fan names (fans.json), handing fans back to the BIOS, drivers, hardware check
 *   sources.php   temperature sources and fan curves
 *   service.php   starting/stopping the service (and loading drivers), fan tests in progress
 */

const PFC_NAME       = 'pwm.fan.control';
const PFC_PLUGIN     = '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/' . PFC_NAME;
const PFC_BOOT       = '/boot/config/plugins/' . PFC_NAME;
const PFC_CONFIG     = PFC_BOOT . '/config.json';
const PFC_FANS       = PFC_BOOT . '/fans.json';
const PFC_CRON       = PFC_BOOT . '/' . PFC_NAME . '.cron';
const PFC_RUN        = '/tmp/' . PFC_NAME;
const PFC_STATUS     = PFC_RUN . '/status.json';
const PFC_HISTORY    = PFC_RUN . '/history.json';
const PFC_FANTEST    = PFC_RUN . '/fantest.json';
const PFC_STOP_FLAG  = PFC_RUN . '/fantest.stop';
const PFC_NV_CACHE   = PFC_RUN . '/nvidia.json';
const PFC_HW_CACHE   = PFC_RUN . '/hardware.json';
const PFC_ALERTS     = PFC_RUN . '/alerts.json';         // warnings and the alerts sent for them
const PFC_NOTIFY_LIMITS = PFC_RUN . '/notify-limits.json'; // rate limits of service alerts
const PFC_PIDFILE    = '/var/run/' . PFC_NAME . '.pid';
const PFC_RC         = PFC_PLUGIN . '/scripts/rc.pwmfancontrol';
const PFC_HWMON      = '/sys/class/hwmon';
const PFC_NVIDIA_SMI = '/usr/bin/nvidia-smi';
const PFC_EMHTTP     = '/var/local/emhttp';
const PFC_NOTIFY     = '/usr/local/emhttp/webGui/scripts/notify';
const PFC_UPDATE_CRON = '/usr/local/sbin/update_cron';
const PFC_CMDLINE    = '/proc/cmdline';
const PFC_MODULES    = '/sys/module';
const PFC_UPTIME     = '/proc/uptime';
const PFC_DMESG      = 'dmesg';
const PFC_MODPROBE   = 'modprobe';

const PFC_OLD_BOOT   = '/boot/config/plugins/array.fan.control';
const PFC_OLD_PLUGIN = '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/array.fan.control';

const PFC_HISTORY_MAX   = 1440;  // samples
const PFC_HISTORY_EVERY = 60;    // seconds between samples (24 hours in total)
const PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM  = 255;
const PFC_INTERVALS     = [2, 3, 5, 10, 15, 30];

require_once __DIR__ . '/config.php';
require_once __DIR__ . '/hardware.php';
require_once __DIR__ . '/sources.php';
require_once __DIR__ . '/service.php';

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ helpers */

function pfc_read_int(string $file): ?int {
    $v = @file_get_contents($file);
    return ($v === false || !is_numeric(trim($v))) ? null : (int)trim($v);
}

function pfc_read_json(string $file, $default = null) {
    if (!is_file($file)) return $default;
    $data = json_decode((string)@file_get_contents($file), true);
    return $data ?? $default;
}

/**
 * Writes a file so readers never see it half written. With $only_if_changed the write is skipped
 * when the content is the same, which saves writes to the flash drive.
 */
function pfc_write_atomic(string $file, string $content, bool $only_if_changed = false): bool {
    if ($only_if_changed && is_file($file) && @file_get_contents($file) === $content) return true;
    @mkdir(dirname($file), 0777, true);
    $tmp = $file . '.tmp' . getmypid();
    if (@file_put_contents($tmp, $content) === false) return false;
    return @rename($tmp, $file);
}

/** JSON in /tmp (status, history, ...): compact. */
function pfc_write_json(string $file, $data): bool {
    return pfc_write_atomic($file, json_encode($data, JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES | JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE));
}

/** JSON on the flash drive (settings): readable, and only written when it changed. */
function pfc_write_flash_json(string $file, $data): bool {
    return pfc_write_atomic($file, json_encode($data, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT | JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES | JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE) . "\n", true);
}

function pfc_log(string $msg): void {
    exec('logger -t ' . escapeshellarg(PFC_NAME) . ' ' . escapeshellarg($msg));
}

/** The server name set in Settings / Identification, or the host name. */
function pfc_server_name(): string {
    $var = @parse_ini_file(PFC_EMHTTP . '/var.ini');
    $name = trim((string)($var['NAME'] ?? ''));
    return $name !== '' ? $name : (string)gethostname();
}

/**
 * Unraid notification, if enabled in the settings. $level: normal|warning|alert.
 * Problems are sent as "alert" (shown in red), resolved problems as "normal".
 * The server name is in the title and the subject (like Unraid's own notifications), so it shows on every agent:
 *   PWM Fan Control - Kaya
 *   [KAYA] PWM Fan Control: Fan problem
 */
function pfc_notify(string $subject, string $description, string $level = 'alert'): void {
    if (!is_executable(PFC_NOTIFY) || !pfc_load_config()['notify']) return;
    $server = pfc_server_name();
    $event = $server !== '' ? "PWM Fan Control - $server" : 'PWM Fan Control';
    $tag = $server !== '' ? '[' . strtoupper($server) . '] ' : '';
    exec(escapeshellarg(PFC_NOTIFY) . ' -e ' . escapeshellarg($event) . ' -s ' . escapeshellarg("{$tag}PWM Fan Control: $subject")
        . ' -d ' . escapeshellarg($description) . ' -i ' . escapeshellarg($level) . ' >/dev/null 2>&1');
}

/**
 * A notification that is sent at most once per $every seconds for the same $key, e.g. for a service
 * that keeps crashing. Used by the service and the watchdog (rc.pwmfancontrol).
 */
function pfc_notify_limited(string $key, string $subject, string $description, int $every = 3600): void {
    $limits = pfc_read_json(PFC_NOTIFY_LIMITS, []);
    if (!is_array($limits)) $limits = [];
    if (time() - (int)($limits[$key] ?? 0) < $every) return;
    $limits[$key] = time();
    pfc_write_json(PFC_NOTIFY_LIMITS, $limits);
    pfc_notify($subject, $description);
}

function pfc_pid_alive($pid): bool {
    return is_numeric($pid) && (int)$pid > 0 && is_dir('/proc/' . (int)$pid);
}

/** Seconds since the server booted (a large number when unknown). */
function pfc_uptime(): float {
    $up = explode(' ', trim((string)@file_get_contents(PFC_UPTIME)))[0] ?? '';
    return is_numeric($up) ? (float)$up : PHP_INT_MAX;
}

/** PWM value (0-255) as a percentage. */
function pfc_pct($pwm): int {
    return (int)round((int)$pwm * 100 / 255);
}

function pfc_fmt_temp($t): string {
    return $t === null ? 'n/a' : rtrim(rtrim(number_format((float)$t, 1, '.', ''), '0'), '.') . '°C';
}

/** Trims a user supplied name to plain text, max 40 characters. */
function pfc_clean_label($label): string {
    $label = trim(strip_tags((string)$label));
    return function_exists('mb_substr') ? mb_substr($label, 0, 40) : substr($label, 0, 40);
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/config.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - settings and fan groups (config.json on the flash drive).
 *
 * {
 *   "enabled": false, "interval": 5, "log_changes": false, "notify": true, "drivers": "nct6775",
 *   "identify": {"low_pwm": 51, "seconds": 8},
 *   "array": {"include": {"Parity": true, ...}, "exclude": ["disk3"], "parity_full_speed": true},
 *   "groups": [{"id": "g1a2b", "name": "Array fans", "fans": ["<fan key>"], "ramp_down": 30,
 *               "sources": [{"source": "array", "low": 35, "high": 48, "min_pwm": 170, "max_pwm": 255, "idle_pwm": 170}]}]
 * }
 * Speeds are stored as PWM values (0-255). The web UI shows them as percentages.
 */

function pfc_default_config(): array {
    return [
        'enabled'     => false,
        'interval'    => 5,
        'log_changes' => false,
        'notify'      => true,
        'drivers'     => '',      // kernel modules to load, e.g. "nct6775" or "it87 force_id=0x8628; nct6775"
        'identify'    => ['low_pwm' => 51, 'seconds' => 8],   // 20%: slows fans clearly without stopping them
        'array'       => [
            // Only read when converting an older config (see pfc_migrate_disk_sources)
            'include' => ['Parity' => true, 'Data' => true, 'Cache' => true, 'Unassigned' => true, 'Flash' => false],
            'exclude' => [],                // disks not used by their disk source
            'parity_full_speed' => true,    // the Array source asks for max speed during a parity check
        ],
        'groups'      => [],
        'disk_sources' => 2,                // 1: older configs, one "array" source for every disk
    ];
}

/** Default curve for a new source binding, depending on the kind of source. */
function pfc_default_binding(string $source): array {
    if ($source === 'array' || $source === 'unassigned') return ['source' => $source, 'low' => 35, 'high' => 48, 'min_pwm' => 170, 'max_pwm' => 255, 'idle_pwm' => 170];
    if (pfc_is_disk_source($source)) return ['source' => $source, 'low' => 45, 'high' => 65, 'min_pwm' => 90, 'max_pwm' => 255, 'idle_pwm' => 90]; // SSD/NVMe pools, flash
    if (strpos($source, 'nvidia:') === 0) return ['source' => $source, 'low' => 45, 'high' => 75, 'min_pwm' => 90, 'max_pwm' => 255];
    return ['source' => $source, 'low' => 40, 'high' => 70, 'min_pwm' => 90, 'max_pwm' => 255];
}

function pfc_load_config(): array {
    $saved = pfc_read_json(PFC_CONFIG);
    if (!is_array($saved)) return pfc_default_config();
    $cfg = pfc_normalize_config($saved);
    if ($cfg['disk_sources'] < 2) {
        // Needs Unraid's disk list to know the pools. Until emhttp has written it, the config is used as it is.
        $disks = pfc_read_disks($cfg);
        if ($disks) {
            $cfg = pfc_migrate_disk_sources($cfg, $disks);
            pfc_save_config($cfg);
        }
    }
    return $cfg;
}

/**
 * Converts a config from before the disk sources were split. The single "array" source covered every
 * disk type ticked under "Disk types to monitor". Every group that used it now gets the Array source
 * and a source for each pool (and unassigned/flash disks) that was ticked, all with the same curve, so
 * the fans behave as before until the curves are changed.
 */
function pfc_migrate_disk_sources(array $cfg, array $disks): array {
    $include = $cfg['array']['include'];
    $present = [];
    // Only sources with a disk the old source used: a pool whose disks were all unticked stays out
    foreach ($disks as $d) if ($d['included']) $present[$d['source']] = true;
    $wanted = [];
    if ($include['Parity'] || $include['Data']) $wanted[] = 'array';
    foreach (array_keys($present) as $id) {
        if (strpos($id, 'pool:') === 0 && $include['Cache']) $wanted[] = $id;
        if ($id === 'unassigned' && $include['Unassigned']) $wanted[] = $id;
        if ($id === 'flash' && $include['Flash']) $wanted[] = $id;
    }
    if (!$wanted) $wanted = ['array'];
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as &$g) {
        $new = [];
        foreach ($g['sources'] as $b) {
            foreach ($b['source'] === 'array' ? $wanted : [$b['source']] as $id) {
                if (!isset($new[$id])) $new[$id] = ['source' => $id] + $b;
            }
        }
        $g['sources'] = array_values($new);
        $names = implode(', ', array_map('pfc_disk_source_name', array_filter(array_column($g['sources'], 'source'), 'pfc_is_disk_source')));
        if ($names !== '') pfc_log("Group \"{$g['name']}\": disk temperatures are now separate sources ($names), with the curve of the former Array disks source");
    }
    unset($g);
    $cfg['disk_sources'] = 2;
    return $cfg;
}

/** Fixes types and fills in defaults, so the rest of the code can trust the structure. */
function pfc_normalize_config(array $cfg): array {
    $out = pfc_default_config();
    foreach (['enabled', 'log_changes', 'notify'] as $k) {
        if (array_key_exists($k, $cfg)) $out[$k] = !empty($cfg[$k]);
    }
    if (isset($cfg['interval'])) $out['interval'] = (int)$cfg['interval'];
    if (isset($cfg['drivers']) && is_string($cfg['drivers'])) {
        $out['drivers'] = implode('; ', array_filter(array_map(fn($e) => preg_replace('/\s+/', ' ', trim($e)), explode(';', $cfg['drivers'])), 'strlen'));
    }
    foreach (['low_pwm', 'seconds'] as $k) {
        if (isset($cfg['identify'][$k]) && is_numeric($cfg['identify'][$k])) $out['identify'][$k] = (int)$cfg['identify'][$k];
    }

    $array = is_array($cfg['array'] ?? null) ? $cfg['array'] : [];
    if (is_array($array['include'] ?? null)) {
        foreach ($out['array']['include'] as $type => $_) $out['array']['include'][$type] = !empty($array['include'][$type]);
    }
    $exclude = is_array($array['exclude'] ?? null) ? $array['exclude'] : [];
    $out['array']['exclude'] = array_values(array_unique(array_filter(array_map('strval', $exclude), 'strlen')));
    if (array_key_exists('parity_full_speed', $array)) $out['array']['parity_full_speed'] = !empty($array['parity_full_speed']);
    $out['disk_sources'] = (int)($cfg['disk_sources'] ?? 1);

    foreach (is_array($cfg['groups'] ?? null) ? $cfg['groups'] : [] as $g) {
        if (!is_array($g)) continue;
        $group = [
            'id'        => preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9_-]/i', '', (string)($g['id'] ?? '')) ?: pfc_new_id(),
            'name'      => pfc_clean_label($g['name'] ?? ''),
            'fans'      => array_values(array_unique(array_map('strval', is_array($g['fans'] ?? null) ? $g['fans'] : []))),
            'ramp_down' => (int)($g['ramp_down'] ?? 30),
            'sources'   => [],
        ];
        foreach (is_array($g['sources'] ?? null) ? $g['sources'] : [] as $b) {
            if (!is_array($b) || empty($b['source'])) continue;
            $defaults = pfc_default_binding((string)$b['source']);
            $binding = ['source' => (string)$b['source']];
            foreach (['low', 'high', 'min_pwm', 'max_pwm', 'idle_pwm'] as $k) {
                if (array_key_exists($k, $defaults)) $binding[$k] = isset($b[$k]) && is_numeric($b[$k]) ? (int)round((float)$b[$k]) : $defaults[$k];
            }
            $group['sources'][] = $binding;
        }
        $out['groups'][] = $group;
    }
    return $out;
}

/** Returns a list of human readable problems. Empty list = valid. */
function pfc_validate_config(array $cfg): array {
    $errors = [];
    if (!in_array($cfg['interval'], PFC_INTERVALS, true)) $errors[] = 'Check interval must be one of ' . implode(', ', PFC_INTERVALS) . ' seconds.';
    if ($cfg['identify']['low_pwm'] < 0 || $cfg['identify']['low_pwm'] > 255) $errors[] = 'Identify speed must be between 0% and 100%.';
    if ($cfg['identify']['seconds'] < 3 || $cfg['identify']['seconds'] > 30) $errors[] = 'Identify duration must be between 3 and 30 seconds.';
    if (pfc_driver_list($cfg) === null) $errors[] = 'Drivers to load: use module names with optional options, separated by ";", e.g. "it87 force_id=0x8628; nct6775".';

    $owner = [];
    $ids = [];
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) {
        $n = $g['name'] !== '' ? $g['name'] : 'Unnamed group';
        if ($g['name'] === '') $errors[] = 'Every group needs a name.';
        if (isset($ids[$g['id']])) $errors[] = "Group \"$n\" has a duplicate id.";
        $ids[$g['id']] = true;
        if ($g['ramp_down'] < 0 || $g['ramp_down'] > 600) $errors[] = "\"$n\": slow-down delay must be between 0 and 600 seconds.";
        if ($g['fans'] && !$g['sources']) $errors[] = "\"$n\": add at least one temperature source.";
        foreach ($g['fans'] as $fan) {
            if (isset($owner[$fan])) $errors[] = "Fan $fan is in both \"{$owner[$fan]}\" and \"$n\". A fan can only be in one group.";
            $owner[$fan] = $n;
        }
        $seen = [];
        foreach ($g['sources'] as $b) {
            if (isset($seen[$b['source']])) $errors[] = "\"$n\": the same source is added twice.";
            $seen[$b['source']] = true;
            if ($b['low'] < -20 || $b['high'] > 150) $errors[] = "\"$n\": temperatures must be between -20 and 150 °C.";
            if ($b['low'] >= $b['high']) $errors[] = "\"$n\": low temperature ({$b['low']} °C) must be below high temperature ({$b['high']} °C).";
            if ($b['min_pwm'] < 0 || $b['max_pwm'] > 255 || $b['min_pwm'] > $b['max_pwm']) {
                $errors[] = "\"$n\": min speed (" . pfc_pct($b['min_pwm']) . '%) must not be above max speed (' . pfc_pct($b['max_pwm']) . '%), within 0-100%.';
            }
            if (isset($b['idle_pwm']) && ($b['idle_pwm'] < 0 || $b['idle_pwm'] > 255)) $errors[] = "\"$n\": spun-down speed must be between 0% and 100%.";
        }
    }
    return array_values(array_unique($errors));
}

function pfc_save_config(array $cfg): bool {
    return pfc_write_flash_json(PFC_CONFIG, $cfg);
}

function pfc_new_id(): string {
    return 'g' . bin2hex(random_bytes(4));
}

/** All fan keys that belong to a group, mapped to the group id. */
function pfc_controlled_keys(array $cfg): array {
    $keys = [];
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) foreach ($g['fans'] as $f) $keys[$f] = $g['id'];
    return $keys;
}

/**
 * The "drivers" setting as [module => [options]], or null when it is not valid.
 * Only plain module names and name=value options are accepted, nothing else reaches modprobe.
 */
function pfc_driver_list(array $cfg): ?array {
    $list = [];
    foreach (explode(';', $cfg['drivers']) as $entry) {
        $parts = preg_split('/\s+/', trim($entry), -1, PREG_SPLIT_NO_EMPTY);
        if (!$parts) continue;
        $module = array_shift($parts);
        if (!preg_match('/^[a-z0-9_-]{1,64}$/i', $module)) return null;
        foreach ($parts as $p) if (!preg_match('/^[a-z0-9_]{1,64}=[a-z0-9_.,:-]{1,64}$/i', $p)) return null;
        $list[$module] = $parts;
    }
    return $list;
}

/** Whether any group follows a GPU (only then nvidia-smi has to run). */
function pfc_uses_nvidia(array $cfg): bool {
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) foreach ($g['sources'] as $b) if (strpos($b['source'], 'nvidia:') === 0) return true;
    return false;
}

/**
 * One-time import of settings from the earlier "Array Fan Control" plugin:
 * fan names/pairings and an "Array fans" group with the old curve.
 */
function pfc_migrate_old(): bool {
    if (is_file(PFC_CONFIG) || !is_dir(PFC_OLD_BOOT)) return false;
    $old = @parse_ini_file(PFC_OLD_BOOT . '/array.fan.control.cfg') ?: [];
    $old_fans = pfc_read_json(PFC_OLD_BOOT . '/fans.json', []);

    $yes = fn($k, $d) => ($old[$k] ?? $d) === 'yes';
    $cfg = [
        'enabled' => false, // stays off until the old plugin is removed, so the two never fight over the fans
        'log_changes' => $yes('LOG_CHANGES', 'no'),
        'identify' => ['low_pwm' => (int)($old['IDENTIFY_LOW_PWM'] ?? 51), 'seconds' => (int)($old['IDENTIFY_SECONDS'] ?? 8)],
        'array' => [
            'include' => [
                'Parity' => $yes('INCLUDE_PARITY', 'yes'), 'Data' => $yes('INCLUDE_DATA', 'yes'), 'Cache' => $yes('INCLUDE_CACHE', 'yes'),
                'Unassigned' => $yes('INCLUDE_UNASSIGNED', 'yes'), 'Flash' => $yes('INCLUDE_FLASH', 'no'),
            ],
            'exclude' => array_values(array_filter(array_map('trim', explode(',', $old['EXCLUDE_DISKS'] ?? '')))),
            'parity_full_speed' => $yes('PARITY_FULL_SPEED', 'yes'),
        ],
        'groups' => [],
    ];

    $fans = ['pwm' => [], 'rpm' => is_array($old_fans['rpm'] ?? null) ? $old_fans['rpm'] : [], 'temp' => []];
    $controlled = [];
    foreach (is_array($old_fans['pwm'] ?? null) ? $old_fans['pwm'] : [] as $key => $f) {
        $fans['pwm'][$key] = array_intersect_key((array)$f, ['label' => 1, 'rpm' => 1, 'orig_enable' => 1]);
        if (!empty($f['controlled'])) $controlled[] = $key;
    }
    $cfg['groups'][] = [
        'id' => pfc_new_id(), 'name' => 'Array fans', 'fans' => $controlled, 'ramp_down' => 0,
        'sources' => [[
            'source' => 'array', 'low' => (int)($old['LOW_TEMP'] ?? 35), 'high' => (int)($old['HIGH_TEMP'] ?? 48),
            'min_pwm' => (int)($old['MIN_PWM'] ?? 170), 'max_pwm' => (int)($old['MAX_PWM'] ?? 255), 'idle_pwm' => (int)($old['IDLE_PWM'] ?? 170),
        ]],
    ];
    pfc_save_config(pfc_normalize_config($cfg));
    pfc_save_fans($fans);
    return true;
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/controller.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - the control loop run by scripts/daemon.php.
 *
 * Every <interval> seconds tick() reads the temperature sources, works out the speed for every fan
 * group and applies it. Speeding up happens right away. Slowing down only happens once the lower
 * speed has been wanted for <ramp_down> seconds (the group keeps the highest speed asked for in that
 * window), so short temperature dips don't make the fans pulse.
 *
 * Safety rules
 *   - A source that can't be read on two checks in a row makes its groups run at full speed.
 *     Exception: disks that just spun up get SPINUP_GRACE seconds for Unraid to read their temperature.
 *   - An error in the loop itself sets every controlled fan to full speed and is retried next check.
 *   - A crash of the service leaves the fans at full speed until the watchdog restarts it.
 *   - Only a deliberate stop (disabled, removed, signal) hands the fans back to the BIOS.
 *
 * It also watches for problems and reports them as warnings (status page, syslog, Unraid alert
 * notifications):
 *   - a fan that stays at 0 RPM while it should spin (needs a confirmed RPM sensor),
 *   - a fan that runs clearly faster or slower than its speed test measured at the same speed, which
 *     usually means a different fan is now connected to that header (fans were moved),
 *   - a fan whose speed or mode is changed by something else (another fan control),
 *   - fans that can't be found or written (driver not loaded, hardware changed),
 *   - temperature sources that can't be read, and errors of the service itself.
 */
final class PfcController {
    private const SOURCE_RETRIES = 1;     // failed reads of a source tolerated before full speed
    private const SPINUP_GRACE   = 600;   // disks that spun up may go this long without a temperature (Unraid can take minutes)
    private const STALL_SECONDS  = 20;    // 0 RPM for this long while it should spin = stalled
    private const STALL_MIN_PWM  = 77;    // 30%: below this, without a speed test, 0 RPM may be normal
    private const SETTLE_SECONDS = 15;    // time a fan needs to reach its speed after a change
    private const MISMATCH_SECONDS = 60;  // RPM far from the speed test for this long = different fan
    private const MISMATCH_LOW   = 0.65;  // RPM below 65% ...
    private const MISMATCH_HIGH  = 1.5;   // ... or above 150% of the speed test = mismatch
    private const CONFLICT_TICKS = 2;     // checks in a row a fan has to be changed by someone else
    private const NOTIFY_AFTER   = 60;    // seconds a warning has to persist before a notification
    private const RESOLVE_SECONDS = 120;  // a warning has to be gone this long to count as resolved
    private const REALERT_AFTER  = 14400; // the same warning is alerted at most once in 4 hours
    private const BOOT_GRACE     = 300;   // no alerts in the first minutes after boot (drivers, array still starting)

    private ?array $cfg = null;
    private ?string $cfgHash = null;
    private array $cfgErrors = [];
    private array $fans = [];
    private ?string $fansHash = null;

    private array $windows = [];      // group id => [[time, pwm], ...] for the slow-down delay
    private array $logged = [];       // group id => last logged pwm
    private array $lastGood = [];     // source id => last good reading
    private array $failures = [];     // source id => failed reads in a row
    private array $waitSince = [];    // disk source id => time its spun-up disks were first seen without a temperature, false = no grace
    private array $written = [];      // fan key => [pwm we set, enable we set]
    private array $conflicts = [];    // fan key => checks in a row changed by someone else
    private array $zeroSince = [];    // fan key => time it was first seen at 0 RPM while it should spin
    private array $setAt = [];        // fan key => [time, pwm] of the last real speed change
    private array $mismatchSince = []; // fan key => time its RPM was first seen far from the speed test
    private ?array $hwCheck = null;   // pfc_hardware_check() while fans are missing, refreshed every minute
    private array $lastWarnings = []; // warnings of the last good check
    private array $alerts;            // see report()
    private int $lastHistory = 0;

    public bool $running = true;

    public function __construct() {
        $this->alerts = self::loadAlerts();
    }

    /** Runs until stopped or disabled, then hands the fans back to the BIOS. */
    public function run(): void {
        pfc_log('Started');
        while ($this->running) {
            $start = microtime(true);
            try {
                if (!$this->tick()) break;
            } catch (Throwable $e) {
                $this->onError($e);
            }
            $interval = $this->cfg['interval'] ?? 5;
            $until = $start + $interval;
            // Sleep until the next check, waking up regularly to notice a stop signal
            while ($this->running && microtime(true) < $until) usleep((int)min(250000, max(1000, ($until - microtime(true)) * 1e6)));
        }
        pfc_release_all($this->cfg);
        @unlink(PFC_STATUS);
        pfc_log('Stopped, fans handed back to the BIOS');
    }

    /** One check. Returns false when fan control was disabled. */
    public function tick(): bool {
        $now = time();
        clearstatcache();
        if (!$this->reload()) return false;

        $cfg = $this->cfg;
        $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
        $nv = pfc_uses_nvidia($cfg) ? pfc_nvidia(max(20, 3 * $cfg['interval'])) : ['available' => false, 'error' => null, 'gpus' => []];
        $sources = $this->withRetries(pfc_read_sources($cfg, $hw, $this->fans, null, $nv), $now);
        $test = pfc_fantest_running();

        $warnings = $nv['error'] ? [$nv['error']] : [];
        $fansChanged = false;
        $groups = [];
        foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) {
            $groups[$g['id']] = $this->controlGroup($g, $sources, $hw, $test, $now, $warnings, $fansChanged);
        }
        if ($fansChanged) $this->saveFans();

        $this->lastWarnings = array_values(array_unique($warnings));
        $this->report($this->lastWarnings, $now);
        $used = $this->usedSources($sources);
        pfc_write_json(PFC_STATUS, [
            'time' => $now, 'pid' => getmypid(), 'interval' => $cfg['interval'],
            'groups' => $groups, 'sources' => $used, 'warnings' => array_values(array_unique($warnings)),
        ]);
        if ($now - $this->lastHistory >= PFC_HISTORY_EVERY) {
            $this->lastHistory = $now;
            $this->recordHistory($now, $used, $groups);
        }
        return true;
    }

    /** Sets every fan we control to full speed. Used after an error and when the service crashes. */
    public function failsafe(): void {
        $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
        $keys = $this->cfg ? array_keys(pfc_controlled_keys($this->cfg)) : [];
        foreach ($this->fans['pwm'] ?? [] as $key => $f) if (isset($f['orig_enable'])) $keys[] = $key;
        foreach (array_unique($keys) as $key) {
            $fan = $hw['pwm'][$key] ?? null;
            if (!$fan) continue;
            if ($fan['enable'] !== null && $fan['enable'] !== 1) @file_put_contents("{$fan['path']}_enable", '1');
            @file_put_contents($fan['path'], (string)PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM);
        }
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- config */

    /** (Re)loads the config and fan names when they changed. Returns false when disabled. */
    private function reload(): bool {
        // Compare content hashes, not mtimes: two saves within one second have the same mtime
        $hash = (string)@md5_file(PFC_CONFIG);
        if ($hash !== $this->cfgHash) {
            $new = pfc_load_config();
            if (!$new['enabled']) return false;
            $errors = pfc_validate_config($new);
            if ($errors) pfc_log('Invalid configuration, all fans run at full speed: ' . implode(' ', $errors));

            // Fans that are no longer in any group go back to the BIOS
            if ($this->cfg) {
                $gone = array_diff_key(pfc_controlled_keys($this->cfg), pfc_controlled_keys($new));
                if ($gone) {
                    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
                    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
                    foreach (array_keys($gone) as $key) {
                        pfc_release_fan($fans, $key, $hw);
                        unset($this->written[$key], $this->conflicts[$key], $this->zeroSince[$key], $this->setAt[$key], $this->mismatchSince[$key]);
                    }
                    pfc_save_fans($fans);
                    $this->fansHash = null;
                }
            }
            $this->cfgHash = $hash;
            $this->cfg = $new;
            $this->cfgErrors = $errors;
            $this->windows = [];
        }
        $hash = (string)@md5_file(PFC_FANS);
        if ($hash !== $this->fansHash) {
            $this->fansHash = $hash;
            $this->fans = pfc_load_fans();
        }
        return true;
    }

    private function saveFans(): void {
        pfc_save_fans($this->fans);
        $this->fansHash = (string)@md5_file(PFC_FANS);
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------ sources */

    /**
     * A single failed read (a sensor glitch, nvidia-smi failing once) uses the previous reading,
     * so it doesn't send the fans to full speed for the whole slow-down delay.
     *
     * Disks that spun up have no temperature until Unraid reads it, which can take minutes. When the
     * source was idle (or the service just started), that is "waiting" for up to SPINUP_GRACE seconds
     * instead of an error. A source that had a temperature and lost it gets no grace.
     */
    private function withRetries(array $sources, int $now): array {
        foreach ($sources as $id => $s) {
            if (empty($s['no_temp'])) {
                unset($this->waitSince[$id]);
            } else {
                if (!isset($this->waitSince[$id])) {
                    $prev = $this->lastGood[$id] ?? null;
                    $this->waitSince[$id] = ($prev === null || $prev['state'] === 'idle') ? $now : false;
                }
                $since = $this->waitSince[$id];
                if ($since !== false && $now - $since < self::SPINUP_GRACE) {
                    $sources[$id] = ['state' => 'waiting', 'detail' => 'disks spun up, waiting for Unraid to read their temperature'] + $s;
                    continue;
                }
            }
            if ($s['state'] !== 'error') {
                $this->failures[$id] = 0;
                $this->lastGood[$id] = $s;
                continue;
            }
            $this->failures[$id] = ($this->failures[$id] ?? 0) + 1;
            if ($this->failures[$id] <= self::SOURCE_RETRIES && isset($this->lastGood[$id])) {
                $sources[$id] = ['detail' => 'last reading, ' . $s['detail']] + $this->lastGood[$id];
            }
        }
        return $sources;
    }

    /** The sources used by a group, for status.json and the history. */
    private function usedSources(array $sources): array {
        $used = [];
        foreach ($this->cfg['groups'] as $g) foreach ($g['sources'] as $b) {
            $s = $sources[$b['source']] ?? null;
            $used[$b['source']] = $s
                ? ['temp' => $s['temp'], 'state' => $s['state'], 'detail' => $s['detail']]
                : ['temp' => null, 'state' => 'error', 'detail' => 'not available'];
        }
        return $used;
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------- groups */

    private function controlGroup(array $g, array $sources, array $hw, ?array $test, int $now, array &$warnings, bool &$fansChanged): array {
        $gid = $g['id'];
        $demand = $this->cfgErrors
            ? ['pwm' => PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM, 'reason' => 'Invalid configuration, running at full speed', 'source' => null, 'demands' => []]
            : pfc_group_demand($g, $sources);
        if ($g['fans']) $this->checkSources($g, $sources, $warnings);

        // Keep the highest demand of the last <ramp_down> seconds
        $this->windows[$gid][] = [$now, $demand['pwm']];
        $this->windows[$gid] = array_values(array_filter($this->windows[$gid], fn($e) => $e[0] >= $now - $g['ramp_down']));
        $pwm = max(array_column($this->windows[$gid], 1));
        $slowDownIn = null;
        if ($pwm > $demand['pwm']) {
            $since = 0;
            foreach ($this->windows[$gid] as $e) if ($e[1] === $pwm) $since = $e[0];
            $slowDownIn = max(0, $since + $g['ramp_down'] - $now);
        }

        $count = 0;
        foreach ($g['fans'] as $key) {
            $name = $this->fanName($key, $hw);
            $fan = $hw['pwm'][$key] ?? null;
            if (!$fan) { $warnings[] = $this->missingFan($key, $name, $g['name'], $hw, $now); continue; }
            if (!$fan['writable']) { $warnings[] = "Fan \"$name\" can't be controlled (not writable)."; continue; }
            $count++;
            if ($test && ($test['key'] ?? '') === $key) {
                // Being tested from the web UI: leave it alone, and don't mistake the test for a conflict
                unset($this->written[$key], $this->zeroSince[$key], $this->setAt[$key], $this->mismatchSince[$key]);
                continue;
            }
            $this->checkConflict($fan, $name, $warnings);
            $error = pfc_drive_fan($this->fans, $fan, $pwm, $fansChanged);
            if ($error) $warnings[] = "Fan \"$name\": $error.";
            $this->written[$key] = [$pwm, 1];
            // Small adjustments don't restart the settle time, the mismatch check is tolerant enough
            if (!isset($this->setAt[$key]) || abs($this->setAt[$key][1] - $pwm) > 13) $this->setAt[$key] = [$now, $pwm];
            $rpmKey = pfc_confirmed_rpm($this->fans, $key);
            $rpm = $rpmKey ? ($hw['rpm'][$rpmKey]['rpm'] ?? null) : null;
            $this->checkStall($key, $name, $pwm, $rpmKey, $rpm, $now, $warnings);
            $this->checkMismatch($key, $name, $pwm, $rpmKey, $rpm, $now, $warnings);
        }
        if ($count) $this->hwCheck = null;

        // Log meaningful changes only (>= 5%, or entering/leaving full speed)
        $prev = $this->logged[$gid] ?? null;
        if ($this->cfg['log_changes'] && $count && ($prev === null || abs($prev - $pwm) >= 13 || ($pwm === 255) !== ($prev === 255))) {
            pfc_log("{$g['name']}: {$demand['reason']}, fans at " . pfc_pct($pwm) . "% ($pwm)");
            $this->logged[$gid] = $pwm;
        }

        return [
            'id' => $gid, 'name' => $g['name'], 'pwm' => $pwm, 'percent' => pfc_pct($pwm),
            'demand' => $demand['pwm'], 'reason' => $demand['reason'], 'source' => $demand['source'],
            'demands' => $demand['demands'], 'slow_down_in' => $slowDownIn, 'fans' => $count,
        ];
    }

    /**
     * Sources of a group that can't be read (after the retry) or no longer exist. The group already runs
     * at full speed then; this makes sure it doesn't go unnoticed, e.g. when the Nvidia driver is gone
     * after an Unraid update. The text has no live values, warnings are tracked by their text.
     */
    private function checkSources(array $g, array $sources, array &$warnings): void {
        foreach ($g['sources'] as $b) {
            $id = $b['source'];
            $s = $sources[$id] ?? null;
            if ($s && $s['state'] !== 'error') continue;
            $label = (string)($this->fans['temp'][$id]['label'] ?? '');
            $name = $s ? pfc_source_name($s) : ($label !== '' ? $label : $this->lastKnownName($id));
            if (!$s) {
                $why = strpos($id, 'nvidia:') === 0 ? 'Is the Nvidia driver loaded and the GPU still installed?'
                    : (pfc_is_disk_source($id) ? 'Does it still have disks assigned? Unraid lists no disks for it.' : 'Is its sensor driver loaded?');
                $warnings[] = "Temperature source \"$name\" of \"{$g['name']}\" was not found, its fans run at full speed. $why";
            } else {
                $warnings[] = "Temperature source \"$name\" of \"{$g['name']}\" can't be read ({$s['detail']}), its fans run at full speed.";
            }
        }
    }

    /** A readable name for a source that is gone: the GPU name nvidia-smi last reported, or its id. */
    private function lastKnownName(string $id): string {
        if (pfc_is_disk_source($id)) return pfc_disk_source_name($id);
        if (strpos($id, 'nvidia:') === 0) {
            foreach (pfc_read_json(PFC_NV_CACHE, [])['gpus'] ?? [] as $gpu) {
                if ('nvidia:' . ($gpu['uuid'] ?? '') === $id) return "GPU {$gpu['index']}: {$gpu['name']}";
            }
        }
        return strpos($id, 'nvidia:') === 0 ? 'GPU ' . substr($id, 7) : $id; // no name known (e.g. after a reboot)
    }

    private function fanName(string $key, array $hw): string {
        $label = (string)($this->fans['pwm'][$key]['label'] ?? '');
        if ($label !== '') return $label;
        $fan = $hw['pwm'][$key] ?? null;
        return $fan ? "{$fan['chip']} PWM {$fan['index']}" : $key;
    }

    /**
     * Something else changed the speed or mode we set (another fan control, the BIOS/EC).
     * Some chips round the value they store, so small differences are ignored.
     */
    private function checkConflict(array $fan, string $name, array &$warnings): void {
        $key = $fan['key'];
        if (!isset($this->written[$key])) return;
        [$pwm] = $this->written[$key];
        $modeChanged = !pfc_is_manual($fan['enable'], $pwm);
        $changed = ($fan['value'] !== null && abs($fan['value'] - $pwm) > 5) || $modeChanged;
        $this->conflicts[$key] = $changed ? ($this->conflicts[$key] ?? 0) + 1 : 0;
        if ($this->conflicts[$key] === self::CONFLICT_TICKS) {
            // Once per episode, what exactly changed: tells another program (speed changed, mode still
            // manual) apart from the BIOS or the chip taking the fan back (mode changed).
            $mode = fn($e) => $e === null ? 'no mode' : ($e === 1 ? 'manual mode (1)' : ($e === 0 ? 'mode 0 (full speed)' : "automatic mode ($e)"));
            $found = ($fan['value'] ?? '?') . ' in ' . $mode($fan['enable']);
            pfc_log("Fan \"$name\" ({$fan['path']}): set to $pwm in manual mode, but found $found. "
                . ($modeChanged
                    ? 'The mode was changed: the BIOS, the chip or another program took the fan back.'
                    : 'The speed was changed while in manual mode: another program writes to this fan.'));
        }
        if ($this->conflicts[$key] >= self::CONFLICT_TICKS) {
            $warnings[] = "Fan \"$name\": its speed keeps being changed by something else. Is another fan control running?";
        }
    }

    /**
     * A fan in a group that isn't there. Says why, as far as we can tell: the chip is missing (driver not
     * loaded, see the hardware check) or the chip is there but not this output (hardware changed).
     */
    private function missingFan(string $key, string $name, string $group, array $hw, int $now): string {
        $chip = strstr($key, '@', true) ?: strstr($key, '/', true);
        $msg = "Fan \"$name\" in \"$group\" was not found, it is not controlled.";
        foreach ($hw['pwm'] as $p) {
            if ($p['chip'] === $chip) return "$msg The $chip chip is there, but not this output: was the hardware or BIOS changed? Add the fan to the group again.";
        }
        if (!$this->hwCheck || $now - $this->hwCheck['time'] >= 60) $this->hwCheck = ['time' => $now] + pfc_hardware_check($hw);
        $hint = pfc_hardware_hint($this->hwCheck, true) ?? "Is the driver for the $chip chip loaded?";
        return "$msg $hint";
    }

    /** A fan that reports 0 RPM for a while although it should spin. Needs a confirmed RPM sensor. */
    private function checkStall(string $key, string $name, int $pwm, ?string $rpmKey, ?int $rpm, int $now, array &$warnings): void {
        // With a speed test we know where the fan starts, otherwise assume it spins from 30%
        $t = $this->speedTest($key, $rpmKey);
        $spinsFrom = $t ? ($t['start_pwm'] ?? $t['min_pwm'] ?? 0) : self::STALL_MIN_PWM;
        if ($rpm === null && $rpmKey && isset($this->zeroSince[$key])) return; // unreadable for a moment: keep counting
        if ($rpm !== 0 || $pwm < max(1, $spinsFrom)) {
            unset($this->zeroSince[$key]);
            return;
        }
        $this->zeroSince[$key] = $this->zeroSince[$key] ?? $now;
        if ($now - $this->zeroSince[$key] >= self::STALL_SECONDS) {
            $warnings[] = "Fan \"$name\" is not spinning (0 RPM). Check the fan and its cable, and whether it was moved to another header.";
        }
    }

    /** The finished speed test of a fan, if it was measured with its current RPM sensor. */
    private function speedTest(string $key, ?string $rpmKey): ?array {
        $t = $this->fans['pwm'][$key]['test'] ?? null;
        return is_array($t) && !empty($t['done']) && ($t['rpm_key'] ?? null) === $rpmKey ? $t : null;
    }

    /**
     * A fan that runs far faster or slower than its speed test measured at the same speed. Fan names and
     * groups belong to the header, so after moving fans to other headers the wrong fans would follow the
     * wrong temperatures without anything failing. Different fan models have quite different speeds, so
     * this catches most mix-ups. Needs a confirmed RPM sensor and a speed test.
     */
    private function checkMismatch(string $key, string $name, int $pwm, ?string $rpmKey, ?int $rpm, int $now, array &$warnings): void {
        $t = $this->speedTest($key, $rpmKey);
        $expected = $t ? pfc_expected_rpm($t['points'] ?? [], $pwm) : null;
        $settled = $now - ($this->setAt[$key][0] ?? $now) >= self::SETTLE_SECONDS;
        if ($rpm === null && isset($this->mismatchSince[$key])) return; // unreadable for a moment: keep counting
        if (!$settled || !$rpm || $expected === null || $expected < 300
            || ($rpm >= $expected * self::MISMATCH_LOW && $rpm <= $expected * self::MISMATCH_HIGH)) {
            unset($this->mismatchSince[$key]);
            return;
        }
        $this->mismatchSince[$key] = $this->mismatchSince[$key] ?? $now;
        if ($now - $this->mismatchSince[$key] >= self::MISMATCH_SECONDS) {
            // Keep the text stable (no live numbers), warnings are tracked by their text
            $warnings[] = "Fan \"$name\" runs much " . ($rpm > $expected ? 'faster' : 'slower') . ' than in its speed test. '
                . 'Was a fan moved to another header? Check with Identify and run the speed test again.';
        }
    }

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------- reporting */

    /**
     * Logs warnings and sends Unraid notifications, without flooding:
     *   - a warning has to last NOTIFY_AFTER seconds before an alert is sent, and is alerted once,
     *   - no alerts in the first BOOT_GRACE seconds after boot, while drivers and the array start,
     *   - it only counts as resolved once it has been gone for RESOLVE_SECONDS, so a problem that comes
     *     and goes stays one problem (one alert, one "resolved" notice),
     *   - the same warning is not alerted again within REALERT_AFTER of its last alert,
     *   - the state is kept in PFC_ALERTS, so a restart of the service doesn't alert again (it is in
     *     /tmp, so after a reboot a problem that still exists is alerted once more).
     */
    private function report(array $warnings, int $now): void {
        $a = &$this->alerts;
        $before = $a;
        foreach (array_unique($warnings) as $w) {
            $e = $a['active'][$w] ?? null;
            if (!$e) {
                pfc_log("Warning: $w");
                $e = ['since' => $now, 'gone' => null, 'handled' => false, 'alerted' => false];
            }
            $e['gone'] = null;
            // During boot the Nvidia driver may still be loading and the array not started yet: warnings are shown,
            // alerts wait until BOOT_GRACE (and are sent then if the problem is still there)
            if (!$e['handled'] && $now - $e['since'] >= self::NOTIFY_AFTER && pfc_uptime() >= self::BOOT_GRACE) {
                $e['handled'] = true;
                if ($now - ($a['sent'][$w] ?? 0) >= self::REALERT_AFTER) {
                    pfc_notify('Fan problem', $w, 'alert');
                    $a['sent'][$w] = $now;
                    $e['alerted'] = true;
                }
            }
            $a['active'][$w] = $e;
        }
        foreach ($a['active'] as $w => $e) {
            if (in_array($w, $warnings, true)) continue;
            if ($e['gone'] === null) { $a['active'][$w]['gone'] = $now; continue; }
            if ($now - $e['gone'] < self::RESOLVE_SECONDS) continue;
            if ($e['alerted']) pfc_notify('Problem resolved', "Back to normal. The problem was: $w", 'normal');
            pfc_log("Resolved: $w");
            unset($a['active'][$w]);
        }
        $a['sent'] = array_filter($a['sent'], fn($t) => $now - $t < self::REALERT_AFTER);
        if ($a !== $before) pfc_write_json(PFC_ALERTS, $a);
    }

    private static function loadAlerts(): array {
        $a = pfc_read_json(PFC_ALERTS, []);
        $active = [];
        foreach (is_array($a['active'] ?? null) ? $a['active'] : [] as $w => $e) {
            if (!is_array($e) || !isset($e['since'])) continue;
            $active[(string)$w] = ['since' => (int)$e['since'], 'gone' => isset($e['gone']) ? (int)$e['gone'] : null,
                'handled' => !empty($e['handled']), 'alerted' => !empty($e['alerted'])];
        }
        $sent = array_map('intval', array_filter(is_array($a['sent'] ?? null) ? $a['sent'] : [], 'is_numeric'));
        return ['active' => $active, 'sent' => $sent];
    }

    private function recordHistory(int $now, array $sources, array $groups): void {
        $history = pfc_read_json(PFC_HISTORY, []);
        $history[] = [
            't' => $now,
            's' => array_map(fn($s) => $s['temp'], $sources),
            'g' => array_map(fn($g) => $g['pwm'], $groups),
        ];
        if (count($history) > PFC_HISTORY_MAX) $history = array_slice($history, -PFC_HISTORY_MAX);
        pfc_write_json(PFC_HISTORY, $history);
    }

    /**
     * An error in the loop: run at full speed, tell the user, try again next check. The warnings of the
     * last good check stay active, so they aren't reported as resolved while the error lasts.
     */
    private function onError(Throwable $e): void {
        $now = time();
        $msg = 'Internal error, fans run at full speed: ' . $e->getMessage() . ' (' . basename($e->getFile()) . ':' . $e->getLine() . ')';
        $this->written = [];
        try { $this->failsafe(); } catch (Throwable $ignored) {}
        $warnings = array_merge($this->lastWarnings, [$msg]);
        try { $this->report($warnings, $now); } catch (Throwable $ignored) {}
        pfc_write_json(PFC_STATUS, ['time' => $now, 'pid' => getmypid(), 'interval' => $this->cfg['interval'] ?? 5,
            'groups' => [], 'sources' => [], 'warnings' => $warnings]);
    }
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/hardware.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - fans and kernel sensors (/sys/class/hwmon), fan names (fans.json), fan drivers and
 * the hardware check.
 *
 * fans.json on the flash drive:
 * {
 *   "pwm":  { "<fan key>":  { "label": "...", "rpm": "<rpm key>|none", "orig_enable": "5", "test": {...} } },
 *   "rpm":  { "<rpm key>":  { "label": "..." } },
 *   "temp": { "<source id>": { "label": "..." } }
 * }
 *   rpm          RPM sensor paired with the output, set by Identify, the speed test or by hand
 *   orig_enable  the BIOS mode of the output before the plugin took it over, restored on release
 *   test         result of the last speed test, see scripts/fantest.php
 */

function pfc_load_fans(): array {
    $data = pfc_read_json(PFC_FANS, []);
    if (!is_array($data)) $data = [];
    foreach (['pwm', 'rpm', 'temp'] as $k) $data[$k] = is_array($data[$k] ?? null) ? $data[$k] : [];
    return $data;
}

function pfc_save_fans(array $fans): bool {
    return pfc_write_flash_json(PFC_FANS, $fans);
}

/**
 * Scans /sys/class/hwmon for PWM outputs, RPM sensors and temperature sensors.
 * Returns ['pwm' => [key => info], 'rpm' => [key => info], 'temp' => [key => info]].
 */
function pfc_scan_hwmon(): array {
    $result = ['pwm' => [], 'rpm' => [], 'temp' => []];
    $used = [];
    $dirs = glob(PFC_HWMON . '/hwmon*') ?: [];
    natsort($dirs);

    foreach ($dirs as $dir) {
        $chip = trim((string)@file_get_contents("$dir/name"));
        if ($chip === '') $chip = basename($dir);
        $device = @realpath("$dir/device");
        $chip_id = $chip . ($device ? '@' . basename($device) : '');
        if (isset($used[$chip_id])) $chip_id .= '#' . basename($dir);
        $used[$chip_id] = true;

        foreach (glob("$dir/fan*_input") ?: [] as $file) {
            if (!preg_match('/\/fan(\d+)_input$/', $file, $m)) continue;
            $n = (int)$m[1];
            $result['rpm']["$chip_id/fan$n"] = [
                'key' => "$chip_id/fan$n", 'chip' => $chip, 'index' => $n, 'path' => $file,
                'driver_label' => trim((string)@file_get_contents("$dir/fan{$n}_label")),
                'rpm' => pfc_read_int($file),
            ];
        }

        // Disk temperatures come from Unraid (the disk sources). Reading drivetemp sensors directly
        // sends commands to the disks, which can keep them from spinning down.
        if ($chip !== 'drivetemp') {
            foreach (glob("$dir/temp*_input") ?: [] as $file) {
                if (!preg_match('/\/temp(\d+)_input$/', $file, $m)) continue;
                $n = (int)$m[1];
                $milli = pfc_read_int($file);
                $result['temp']["$chip_id/temp$n"] = [
                    'key' => "$chip_id/temp$n", 'chip' => $chip, 'index' => $n, 'path' => $file,
                    'driver_label' => trim((string)@file_get_contents("$dir/temp{$n}_label")),
                    'temp' => $milli === null ? null : round($milli / 1000, 1),
                ];
            }
        }

        foreach (glob("$dir/pwm*") ?: [] as $file) {
            if (!preg_match('/\/pwm(\d+)$/', $file, $m)) continue;
            $n = (int)$m[1];
            $result['pwm']["$chip_id/pwm$n"] = [
                'key' => "$chip_id/pwm$n", 'chip' => $chip, 'index' => $n, 'path' => $file, 'hwmon' => basename($dir),
                'value'  => pfc_read_int($file),
                'enable' => is_file("{$file}_enable") ? pfc_read_int("{$file}_enable") : null,
                'mode'   => is_file("{$file}_mode") ? pfc_read_int("{$file}_mode") : null, // 0 = DC, 1 = PWM
                'writable'  => is_writable($file),
                // Most drivers pair pwmN with fanN_input, but this is only a guess
                'guess_rpm' => isset($result['rpm']["$chip_id/fan$n"]) ? "$chip_id/fan$n" : null,
            ];
        }
    }
    foreach ($result as &$list) uksort($list, 'strnatcmp');
    unset($list);
    return $result;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------- drivers and setup */

// Drivers of motherboard/controller chips that offer PWM fan outputs
const PFC_FAN_DRIVERS = ['nct6775', 'nct6683', 'nct6687', 'it87', 'f71882fg', 'f71805f', 'w83627ehf', 'w83627hf', 'w83795',
    'sch5627', 'sch5636', 'asus_ec_sensors', 'dell_smm_hwmon', 'thinkpad_acpi', 'applesmc', 'pwm_fan', 'emc2305', 'max6650'];

/** Loads the kernel modules from the "drivers" setting that aren't loaded yet. Returns the errors. */
function pfc_load_drivers(array $cfg): array {
    $errors = [];
    foreach (pfc_driver_list($cfg) ?? [] as $module => $options) {
        if (is_dir(PFC_MODULES . '/' . str_replace('-', '_', $module))) continue;
        exec(PFC_MODPROBE . ' ' . implode(' ', array_map('escapeshellarg', array_merge([$module], $options))) . ' 2>&1', $out, $rc);
        if ($rc !== 0) {
            $errors[] = "Could not load driver $module" . ($out ? ': ' . trim(implode(' ', $out)) : '');
            pfc_log(end($errors));
        } else {
            pfc_log("Loaded driver $module");
        }
        $out = [];
    }
    if (!$errors) @unlink(PFC_HW_CACHE);
    return $errors;
}

/**
 * Checks what is needed to control fans, for the hardware check in the web UI and for warnings:
 *   drivers      loaded fan controller drivers
 *   lax          acpi_enforce_resources=lax is on the kernel command line
 *   conflicts    kernel log lines about ACPI resource conflicts (the reason "lax" is needed)
 *   pwm/writable number of PWM outputs found / writable
 * The kernel log part is cached for a minute, it can be large.
 */
function pfc_hardware_check(?array $hw = null): array {
    $hw = $hw ?? pfc_scan_hwmon();
    $cache = pfc_read_json(PFC_HW_CACHE);
    if (!is_array($cache) || time() - ($cache['time'] ?? 0) > 60) {
        exec(PFC_DMESG . ' 2>/dev/null', $log);
        $conflicts = [];
        foreach ($log as $line) {
            if (preg_match('/conflicts with OpRegion|resource conflict|acpi_enforce_resources/i', $line)) $conflicts[] = trim($line);
        }
        $cache = ['time' => time(), 'conflicts' => array_slice(array_values(array_unique($conflicts)), -6)];
        pfc_write_json(PFC_HW_CACHE, $cache);
    }
    return [
        'drivers'   => array_values(array_filter(PFC_FAN_DRIVERS, fn($m) => is_dir(PFC_MODULES . "/$m"))),
        'lax'       => (bool)preg_match('/(^|\s)acpi_enforce_resources=lax(\s|$)/', (string)@file_get_contents(PFC_CMDLINE)),
        'conflicts' => $cache['conflicts'],
        'pwm'       => count($hw['pwm']),
        'writable'  => count(array_filter($hw['pwm'], fn($p) => $p['writable'])),
    ];
}

/**
 * What to do when fans can't be found or controlled, based on pfc_hardware_check(). Null if all looks fine.
 * $missing: a fan in a group is missing although other outputs work (its chip may be the one in conflict).
 */
function pfc_hardware_hint(array $check, bool $missing = false): ?string {
    if ($check['conflicts'] && !$check['lax'] && ($missing || !$check['writable'])) {
        return 'The kernel log shows an ACPI resource conflict, which keeps the fan driver from using the chip. '
            . 'Add acpi_enforce_resources=lax to the boot options (Main > Flash > Syslinux Configuration, on the "append" line) and reboot.';
    }
    if (!$check['drivers']) {
        return 'No fan controller driver is loaded. Enter it under "Drivers to load" in the settings (e.g. nct6775 or it87), '
            . 'or let the Dynamix System Temperature plugin load it.';
    }
    if (!$check['pwm']) {
        return 'The driver ' . implode(', ', $check['drivers']) . ' is loaded but offers no fan outputs. '
            . ($check['lax'] ? 'Your board may need a different driver.' : 'Your board may need acpi_enforce_resources=lax in the boot options, or a different driver.');
    }
    if (!$check['writable']) return 'Fan outputs were found but none can be written. The plugin has to run as root.';
    return null;
}

function pfc_enable_mode_name($enable): string {
    $names = [0 => 'Full speed', 1 => 'Manual', 2 => 'Thermal cruise', 3 => 'Fan speed cruise', 4 => 'Smart Fan III', 5 => 'Smart Fan IV'];
    return $enable === null ? 'n/a' : ($names[$enable] ?? "Mode $enable");
}

/** The RPM sensor confirmed for a fan (by Identify, the speed test or by hand), or null. */
function pfc_confirmed_rpm(array $fans, string $key): ?string {
    $rpm = $fans['pwm'][$key]['rpm'] ?? null;
    return is_string($rpm) && $rpm !== 'none' ? $rpm : null;
}

/**
 * The RPM a speed test measured at $pwm, interpolated between its steps. Null below the lowest
 * speed the fan kept running at, where it may be stopped.
 */
function pfc_expected_rpm(array $points, int $pwm): ?float {
    $running = array_values(array_filter($points, fn($p) => is_array($p) && (int)($p[1] ?? 0) > 0));
    if (!$running) return null;
    usort($running, fn($a, $b) => $a[0] <=> $b[0]);
    if ($pwm < $running[0][0]) return null;
    $prev = $running[0];
    foreach ($running as $p) {
        if ($pwm <= $p[0]) {
            return $p[0] === $prev[0] ? (float)$p[1] : $prev[1] + ($p[1] - $prev[1]) * ($pwm - $prev[0]) / ($p[0] - $prev[0]);
        }
        $prev = $p;
    }
    return (float)$prev[1];
}

/**
 * Whether an output in mode $enable is under manual control at speed $pwm. The nct6775 driver reports
 * manual mode at 255 as mode 0 ("full speed"), so that counts as manual too.
 */
function pfc_is_manual(?int $enable, int $pwm): bool {
    return $enable === null || $enable === 1 || ($enable === 0 && $pwm === 255);
}

/**
 * Switches an output to manual control and sets its speed.
 * Remembers the BIOS mode in $fans the first time (returns $changed = true then).
 * Returns null on success, or an error message.
 */
function pfc_drive_fan(array &$fans, array $fan, int $pwm, bool &$changed): ?string {
    $key = $fan['key'];
    if (!pfc_is_manual($fan['enable'], $pwm)) {
        if (!isset($fans['pwm'][$key]['orig_enable'])) {
            $fans['pwm'][$key]['orig_enable'] = (string)$fan['enable'];
            $changed = true;
        }
        if (@file_put_contents("{$fan['path']}_enable", '1') === false) return 'could not switch it to manual control';
    }
    if ($fan['value'] !== $pwm && @file_put_contents($fan['path'], (string)$pwm) === false) return 'could not set its speed';
    return null;
}

/**
 * Puts a fan back under BIOS/driver control (the mode it had before we took it over).
 * Safe to call more than once: a fan that is no longer in manual mode is left alone.
 */
function pfc_release_fan(array &$fans, string $key, array $hw): void {
    $orig = $fans['pwm'][$key]['orig_enable'] ?? null;
    unset($fans['pwm'][$key]['orig_enable']);
    if (!isset($hw['pwm'][$key])) return;
    $fan = $hw['pwm'][$key];
    if ($orig !== null && $orig !== '' && $orig != 1 && is_writable("{$fan['path']}_enable")) {
        @file_put_contents("{$fan['path']}_enable", (string)$orig);
    } elseif ($fan['enable'] === null || $fan['enable'] === 1) {
        // Was already manual before we took it, or has no mode: leave it at full speed to be safe
        @file_put_contents($fan['path'], (string)PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM);
    }
}

/** Releases every fan we control or have taken over. */
function pfc_release_all(?array $cfg = null): void {
    $cfg = $cfg ?? pfc_load_config();
    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
    $hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
    $keys = array_keys(pfc_controlled_keys($cfg));
    foreach ($fans['pwm'] as $key => $f) if (isset($f['orig_enable'])) $keys[] = $key;
    foreach (array_unique($keys) as $key) pfc_release_fan($fans, $key, $hw);
    pfc_save_fans($fans);
}

/** Every PWM output with its name, pairing, group and current RPM, for the web UI. */
function pfc_fan_list(array $cfg, array $fans, array $hw): array {
    $owner = pfc_controlled_keys($cfg);
    $taken = [];  // RPM sensors confirmed for an output can't be another output's guess
    foreach ($hw['pwm'] as $key => $_) if ($r = pfc_confirmed_rpm($fans, $key)) $taken[$r] = $key;
    $list = [];
    foreach ($hw['pwm'] as $key => $p) {
        $f = $fans['pwm'][$key] ?? [];
        if ($p['guess_rpm'] !== null && isset($taken[$p['guess_rpm']]) &&$taken[$p['guess_rpm']] !== $key) $p['guess_rpm'] = null;
        $rpm_key = $f['rpm'] ?? $p['guess_rpm'];
        unset($p['path']);
        $list[] = $p + [
            'label'         => (string)($f['label'] ?? ''),
            'group'         => $owner[$key] ?? null,
            'rpm_key'       => $rpm_key,
            'rpm_confirmed' => isset($f['rpm']),
            'rpm'           => $rpm_key !== null ? ($hw['rpm'][$rpm_key]['rpm'] ?? null) : null,
            'enable_name'   => pfc_enable_mode_name($p['enable']),
            'test'          => $f['test'] ?? null,
        ];
    }
    return $list;
}

/** Every RPM sensor with its name, for the web UI. */
function pfc_rpm_list(array $fans, array $hw): array {
    $list = [];
    foreach ($hw['rpm'] as $key => $r) {
        unset($r['path']);
        $list[] = $r + ['label' => (string)($fans['rpm'][$key]['label'] ?? '')];
    }
    return $list;
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/service.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - the background service (scripts/daemon.php) and fan tests (scripts/fantest.php).
 */

function pfc_daemon_pid(): ?int {
    $pid = (int)trim((string)@file_get_contents(PFC_PIDFILE));
    return pfc_pid_alive($pid) ? $pid : null;
}

/**
 * Loads the configured drivers, then starts or stops the service and its watchdog cron job to match
 * the config. Runs at boot (install.sh) and whenever the settings are saved.
 */
function pfc_apply_service(array $cfg): void {
    pfc_load_drivers($cfg);
    if ($cfg['enabled']) {
        pfc_write_atomic(PFC_CRON, "# PWM Fan Control watchdog (generated, do not edit)\n* * * * * " . PFC_RC . " watchdog >/dev/null 2>&1\n\n", true);
    } else {
        @unlink(PFC_CRON);
    }
    exec(PFC_UPDATE_CRON . ' >/dev/null 2>&1');
    exec(PFC_RC . ($cfg['enabled'] ? ' start' : ' stop') . ' >/dev/null 2>&1');
}

/** The fan test (Identify or speed test) in progress, or null. */
function pfc_fantest_running(): ?array {
    $state = pfc_read_json(PFC_FANTEST);
    if (!is_array($state) || ($state['phase'] ?? '') === 'done') return null;
    // Just requested by the web UI, the script hasn't written its pid yet
    if (($state['phase'] ?? '') === 'starting') return time() - ($state['time'] ?? 0) < 10 ? $state : null;
    return pfc_pid_alive($state['pid'] ?? 0) ? $state : null;
}

/** Starts scripts/fantest.php in the background. $mode: identify|speed. Returns an error or null. */
function pfc_fantest_start(string $key, string $mode): ?string {
    if (pfc_fantest_running()) return 'Another fan test is running right now.';
    @unlink(PFC_STOP_FLAG);
    pfc_write_json(PFC_FANTEST, ['key' => $key, 'mode' => $mode, 'phase' => 'starting', 'pid' => 0, 'time' => time()]);
    exec('setsid nohup /usr/bin/php ' . escapeshellarg(PFC_PLUGIN . '/scripts/fantest.php') . ' ' . escapeshellarg($mode) . ' '
        . escapeshellarg($key) . ' >/dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &');
    return null;
}

/**
 * Why the fan $key can't be tested right now, or null. While a test runs, the service leaves the fan
 * alone, so a test must not start (and is stopped) when the fan's group needs it: one of its
 * temperatures is at or above "high", can't be read, or a parity check runs at full speed. Fans that
 * are in no group are not checked.
 */
function pfc_fan_needed(array $cfg, string $key, ?array $hw = null): ?string {
    $gid = pfc_controlled_keys($cfg)[$key] ?? null;
    $group = null;
    foreach ($cfg['groups'] as $g) if ($g['id'] === $gid) $group = $g;
    if (!$group || !$group['sources']) return null;
    $sources = pfc_read_sources($cfg, $hw ?? pfc_scan_hwmon(), pfc_load_fans());
    foreach ($group['sources'] as $b) {
        $s = $sources[$b['source']] ?? null;
        if (!$s || $s['state'] === 'error') return ($s ? pfc_source_name($s) : $b['source']) . " can't be read";
        if ($s['state'] === 'parity') return 'a parity check is running';
        if ($s['temp'] !== null && $s['temp'] >= $b['high']) {
            return pfc_source_name($s) . ' is at ' . pfc_fmt_temp($s['temp']) . " (high: {$b['high']}°C)";
        }
    }
    return null;
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/include/sources.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - temperature sources and fan curves.
 *
 * A source, as returned by pfc_read_sources():
 *   ['id', 'type' => disk|nvidia|hwmon, 'name' (default name), 'label' (user name), 'temp' => ?float,
 *    'state' => ok|idle|waiting|parity|error, 'detail' => string]
 * "waiting" is only set by the service: disks that just spun up and have no temperature yet.
 */

/**
 * The disk source a disk belongs to: "array" (parity and data disks), "pool:<name>" (one per pool),
 * "unassigned" or "flash". Pool devices are named after their pool ("cache", "cache2", ...), ZFS
 * subpools as "<pool>~<subpool>", so the pool name is the part before "~" without trailing digits.
 */
function pfc_disk_source_id(string $type, string $name): ?string {
    switch ($type) {
        case 'Parity': case 'Data': return 'array';
        case 'Cache': return 'pool:' . preg_replace('/\d+$/', '', explode('~', $name)[0]);
        case 'Unassigned': return 'unassigned';
        case 'Flash': case 'Boot': return 'flash';
    }
    return null;
}

function pfc_is_disk_source(string $id): bool {
    return in_array($id, ['array', 'unassigned', 'flash'], true) || strpos($id, 'pool:') === 0;
}

/** Default name of a disk source. */
function pfc_disk_source_name(string $id): string {
    if (strpos($id, 'pool:') === 0) return 'Pool: ' . substr($id, 5);
    return ['array' => 'Array', 'unassigned' => 'Unassigned disks', 'flash' => 'Flash'][$id] ?? $id;
}

/** Unraid's disks (array, pools and unassigned devices), with the disk source each one belongs to. */
function pfc_read_disks(array $cfg): array {
    $exclude = $cfg['array']['exclude'];
    $disks = [];

    $files = [[PFC_EMHTTP . '/disks.ini', null]];
    foreach ([PFC_EMHTTP . '/devs.ini', '/usr/local/emhttp/state/devs.ini'] as $devs) {
        if (is_file($devs)) { $files[] = [$devs, 'Unassigned']; break; }
    }
    foreach ($files as [$file, $force_type]) {
        $ini = is_file($file) ? @parse_ini_file($file, true) : false;
        if (!is_array($ini)) continue;
        foreach ($ini as $section => $d) {
            if (!is_array($d)) continue;
            $type = $force_type ?? (string)($d['type'] ?? '');
            $temp = trim((string)($d['temp'] ?? ''), '"');
            $disk = [
                'name' => (string)$section, 'type' => $type, 'device' => (string)($d['id'] ?? ''),
                'source' => pfc_disk_source_id($type, (string)$section),
                'temp' => preg_match('/^\d+$/', $temp) ? (int)$temp : null,
                'spundown' => ($d['spundown'] ?? '0') == '1',
                'included' => true, 'reason' => '',
            ];
            if ($disk['device'] === '') { $disk['included'] = false; $disk['reason'] = 'Not assigned'; }
            elseif ($disk['source'] === null) { $disk['included'] = false; $disk['reason'] = "$type disks are not used"; }
            elseif (in_array($disk['name'], $exclude, true)) { $disk['included'] = false; $disk['reason'] = 'Excluded'; }
            $disks[] = $disk;
        }
    }
    return $disks;
}

function pfc_parity_running(): bool {
    $var = @parse_ini_file(PFC_EMHTTP . '/var.ini');
    return is_array($var) && (int)trim((string)($var['mdResync'] ?? '0'), '"') > 0;
}

/** Whether the array is started. Unknown (no var.ini) counts as started. */
function pfc_array_started(): bool {
    $var = @parse_ini_file(PFC_EMHTTP . '/var.ini');
    if (!is_array($var) || !isset($var['mdState'])) return true;
    return trim((string)$var['mdState'], '"') === 'STARTED';
}

/**
 * Nvidia GPUs via nvidia-smi. Returns ['available' => bool, 'error' => ?string, 'gpus' => [...]].
 *
 * nvidia-smi always runs in the background and is never waited on: when a GPU or the driver
 * crashes, nvidia-smi can hang so hard that even "timeout"/SIGKILL can't end it, and a caller
 * waiting on it would freeze fan control. Instead the latest finished result is used. When it
 * is older than $max_age seconds, every GPU is reported without a temperature, which makes the
 * groups using them run at full speed. A new query only starts when the previous one finished.
 */
function pfc_nvidia(int $max_age = 20): array {
    if (!is_executable(PFC_NVIDIA_SMI)) return ['available' => false, 'error' => null, 'gpus' => []];
    @mkdir(PFC_RUN, 0777, true);
    $out = PFC_RUN . '/nvidia.out';
    $rcf = PFC_RUN . '/nvidia.rc';
    $pidf = PFC_RUN . '/nvidia.pid';

    $lock = fopen(PFC_RUN . '/nvidia.lock', 'c');
    if ($lock) flock($lock, LOCK_EX);

    // Picks up the result of a finished run (nvidia.rc appears when it is done)
    $collect = function () use ($out, $rcf, $pidf): bool {
        $claim = $rcf . '.' . getmypid();
        if (!@rename($rcf, $claim)) return false;
        $rc = (int)trim((string)@file_get_contents($claim));
        $lines = array_filter(array_map('trim', explode("\n", (string)@file_get_contents($out))));
        $result = ['time' => (int)@filemtime($claim), 'error' => null, 'gpus' => []];
        if ($rc !== 0) {
            $result['error'] = $rc === 124 || $rc === 137 ? 'nvidia-smi timed out' : 'nvidia-smi failed: ' . implode(' ', array_slice($lines, 0, 2));
        } else {
            foreach ($lines as $line) {
                $p = array_map('trim', str_getcsv($line));
                if (count($p) < 4 || strpos($p[1], 'GPU-') !== 0) continue;
                $result['gpus'][] = ['index' => (int)$p[0], 'uuid' => $p[1], 'name' => $p[2], 'temp' => is_numeric($p[3]) ? (float)$p[3] : null];
            }
        }
        // Keep the GPU list from the last good result, so failing GPUs stay visible (without a temperature)
        if ($result['error']) {
            $prev = pfc_read_json(PFC_NV_CACHE, []);
            $result['gpus'] = array_map(fn($g) => ['temp' => null] + $g, $prev['gpus'] ?? []);
        }
        pfc_write_json(PFC_NV_CACHE, $result);
        @unlink($claim);
        @unlink($pidf);
        return true;
    };
    $launch = function () use ($out, $rcf, $pidf): void {
        $cmd = '(timeout -k 2 5 ' . escapeshellarg(PFC_NVIDIA_SMI) . ' --query-gpu=index,uuid,name,temperature.gpu --format=csv,noheader,nounits'
             . ' > ' . escapeshellarg($out) . ' 2>&1; echo $? > ' . escapeshellarg("$rcf.tmp") . '; mv ' . escapeshellarg("$rcf.tmp") . ' ' . escapeshellarg($rcf) . ')'
             . ' > /dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null & echo $!';
        file_put_contents($pidf, trim((string)shell_exec($cmd)));
    };

    $collect();
    $cache = pfc_read_json(PFC_NV_CACHE);
    $busy = pfc_pid_alive(trim((string)@file_get_contents($pidf))) || is_file($rcf);
    $fresh = is_array($cache) && time() - ($cache['time'] ?? 0) < 2;
    if (!$busy && !$fresh) $launch();

    // Very first call: wait briefly for a result, instead of starting with "no data"
    if (!is_array($cache)) {
        for ($i = 0; $i < 60 && !$collect(); $i++) usleep(100000);
        $cache = pfc_read_json(PFC_NV_CACHE);
    }
    if ($lock) { flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock); }

    $result = ['available' => true, 'error' => $cache['error'] ?? null, 'gpus' => $cache['gpus'] ?? []];
    if (!is_array($cache)) {
        $result['error'] = 'nvidia-smi is not responding';
    } elseif (time() - ($cache['time'] ?? 0) > $max_age) {
        $result['error'] = "nvidia-smi has not answered for more than $max_age seconds";
        $result['gpus'] = array_map(fn($g) => ['temp' => null] + $g, $result['gpus']);
    }
    return $result;
}

/** Reads every available temperature source. Pass $disks/$nv when already read. */
function pfc_read_sources(array $cfg, array $hw, array $fans, ?array $disks = null, ?array $nv = null): array {
    $sources = [];
    $label = fn($id) => (string)($fans['temp'][$id]['label'] ?? '');

    // Disks: one source for the array, one per pool, unassigned devices and the flash drive. Each one
    // is the hottest of its disks that are used and spun up.
    $disks = $disks ?? pfc_read_disks($cfg);
    $bySource = [];
    foreach ($disks as $d) if ($d['device'] !== '' && $d['source'] !== null) $bySource[$d['source']][] = $d;
    uksort($bySource, fn($a, $b) => [pfc_disk_order($a), $a] <=> [pfc_disk_order($b), $b]);
    $parity = null;
    $started = null;
    foreach ($bySource as $id => $list) {
        $included = array_filter($list, fn($d) => $d['included']);
        $active = array_filter($included, fn($d) => !$d['spundown']);
        $hot = null;
        foreach ($active as $d) if ($d['temp'] !== null && ($hot === null || $d['temp'] > $hot['temp'])) $hot = $d;
        // Most flash drives report no temperature: only list it when it does, or when a group uses it
        if ($id === 'flash' && !$hot && !in_array('flash', array_column(array_merge([], ...array_column($cfg['groups'], 'sources')), 'source'), true)) continue;
        $src = ['id' => $id, 'type' => 'disk', 'name' => pfc_disk_source_name($id), 'label' => $label($id), 'temp' => $hot['temp'] ?? null, 'state' => 'ok', 'detail' => $hot ? "hottest is {$hot['name']}" : ''];
        $inArray = $id === 'array' || strpos($id, 'pool:') === 0; // only there while the array is started
        if (!$included) { $src['state'] = 'error'; $src['detail'] = 'all its disks are unticked'; }
        elseif ($id === 'array' && $cfg['array']['parity_full_speed'] && ($parity ??= pfc_parity_running())) { $src['state'] = 'parity'; $src['detail'] = 'parity check/rebuild running'; }
        elseif (!$active) { $src['state'] = 'idle'; $src['detail'] = 'all disks spun down'; }
        // A stopped array (e.g. an encrypted array waiting for its passphrase) has no temperatures: like spun down
        elseif (!$hot && $inArray && !($started ??= pfc_array_started())) { $src['state'] = 'idle'; $src['detail'] = 'array is stopped'; }
        // Disks spun up without a temperature. Right after a spin-up this is normal: Unraid can take minutes to
        // fill in the temperature. The service (PfcController) tolerates it for a while when the source was idle.
        elseif (!$hot) { $src['state'] = 'error'; $src['detail'] = 'no disk temperature available'; $src['no_temp'] = true; }
        $sources[$id] = $src;
    }

    // Nvidia GPUs
    $nv = $nv ?? pfc_nvidia();
    foreach ($nv['gpus'] as $g) {
        $id = 'nvidia:' . $g['uuid'];
        $sources[$id] = [
            'id' => $id, 'type' => 'nvidia', 'name' => "GPU {$g['index']}: {$g['name']}", 'label' => $label($id),
            'temp' => $g['temp'], 'state' => $g['temp'] === null ? 'error' : 'ok',
            'detail' => $g['temp'] === null ? 'temperature not available' : '',
        ];
    }

    // Kernel sensors
    foreach ($hw['temp'] as $key => $t) {
        $id = "hwmon:$key";
        $sources[$id] = [
            'id' => $id, 'type' => 'hwmon', 'name' => $t['chip'] . ' ' . ($t['driver_label'] !== '' ? $t['driver_label'] : "temp{$t['index']}"),
            'label' => $label($id), 'temp' => $t['temp'], 'state' => $t['temp'] === null ? 'error' : 'ok',
            'detail' => $t['temp'] === null ? 'temperature not available' : '',
        ];
    }
    return $sources;
}

/** Sort order of the disk sources: array, pools, unassigned, flash. */
function pfc_disk_order(string $id): int {
    return strpos($id, 'pool:') === 0 ? 1 : (['array' => 0, 'unassigned' => 2, 'flash' => 3][$id] ?? 4);
}

function pfc_source_name(array $src): string {
    return $src['label'] !== '' ? $src['label'] : $src['name'];
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ curves */

/** Linear curve: min_pwm at or below low, max_pwm at or above high. */
function pfc_curve_pwm(float $temp, array $b): int {
    if ($temp <= $b['low']) return (int)$b['min_pwm'];
    if ($temp >= $b['high']) return (int)$b['max_pwm'];
    return (int)round($b['min_pwm'] + ($temp - $b['low']) * ($b['max_pwm'] - $b['min_pwm']) / ($b['high'] - $b['low']));
}

/** Speed one source binding asks for. Returns ['pwm' => int, 'reason' => string]. */
function pfc_binding_demand(array $b, ?array $src): array {
    if (!$src) return ['pwm' => PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM, 'reason' => 'A temperature source is not available, running at full speed'];
    $name = pfc_source_name($src);
    switch ($src['state']) {
        case 'error':  return ['pwm' => PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM, 'reason' => "$name: {$src['detail']}, running at full speed"];
        case 'parity': return ['pwm' => (int)$b['max_pwm'], 'reason' => "$name: {$src['detail']}"];
        case 'idle':   return ['pwm' => (int)($b['idle_pwm'] ?? $b['min_pwm']), 'reason' => "$name: {$src['detail']}"];
        // Just spun up, no temperature yet: the disks were cold, so the lowest curve speed (at least the spun-down speed)
        case 'waiting': return ['pwm' => max((int)$b['min_pwm'], (int)($b['idle_pwm'] ?? $b['min_pwm'])), 'reason' => "$name: {$src['detail']}"];
    }
    return ['pwm' => pfc_curve_pwm($src['temp'], $b), 'reason' => "$name at " . pfc_fmt_temp($src['temp'])];
}

/**
 * What a group wants right now (before the slow-down delay): the highest demand of its sources.
 * Returns ['pwm' => int, 'reason' => string, 'source' => ?id, 'demands' => [id => pwm]].
 */
function pfc_group_demand(array $group, array $sources): array {
    $best = null;
    $demands = [];
    foreach ($group['sources'] as $b) {
        $d = pfc_binding_demand($b, $sources[$b['source']] ?? null);
        $demands[$b['source']] = $d['pwm'];
        if ($best === null || $d['pwm'] > $best['pwm']) $best = $d + ['source' => $b['source']];
    }
    if ($best === null) return ['pwm' => PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM, 'reason' => 'No temperature sources, running at full speed', 'source' => null, 'demands' => []];
    return $best + ['demands' => $demands];
}
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/js/pfc.js">
<INLINE><![CDATA[/* PWM Fan Control - settings page */
(function ($) {
  'use strict';

  const root = document.getElementById('pfc');
  if (!root) return;
  const API = root.dataset.api;
  const CSRF = root.dataset.csrf;
  const COLORS = ['#f0820a', '#3b82f6', '#16a34a', '#a855f7', '#d9534f', '#0891b2'];

  let state = null;       // last response from the server
  let draft = null;       // config being edited
  let dirty = false;
  let history = [];
  let groupsBuilt = false;
  let showUnnamed = false; // group editor: also offer outputs without a name
  let pwmSig = '';
  let rpmSig = '';
  let sourceSig = '';
  let testDismissed = null;
  let timer = null;
  let historyTick = 0;

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ helpers */

  const esc = s => String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;' }[c]));
  const pct = pwm => Math.round(pwm * 100 / 255);
  const toPwm = p => Math.max(0, Math.min(255, Math.round(p * 255 / 100)));
  const clone = o => JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(o));
  const focused = el => el === document.activeElement;
  const fmtTemp = t => (t == null ? 'n/a' : (Math.round(t * 10) / 10) + '°C');

  function getPath(obj, path) { return path.split('.').reduce((o, k) => (o == null ? undefined : o[k]), obj); }
  function setPath(obj, path, value) {
    const keys = path.split('.');
    const last = keys.pop();
    keys.reduce((o, k) => (o[k] = o[k] || {}), obj)[last] = value;
  }

  function post(data) {
    return $.post(API, Object.assign({ csrf_token: CSRF }, data))
      .then(r => (typeof r === 'string' ? JSON.parse(r) : r))
      .then(r => { if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.error || 'Request failed'); return r; },
            xhr => { throw new Error((xhr && xhr.responseJSON && xhr.responseJSON.error) || 'Request failed'); });
  }

  function showError(err) {
    const msg = err && err.message ? err.message : String(err);
    if (typeof swal === 'function') swal({ title: 'PWM Fan Control', text: msg, type: 'error' });
    else alert(msg);
  }

  function ago(ts) {
    if (!ts) return 'never';
    const s = Math.max(0, Math.round(Date.now() / 1000 - ts));
    if (s < 60) return s + 's ago';
    if (s < 3600) return Math.round(s / 60) + ' min ago';
    return new Date(ts * 1000).toLocaleString();
  }

  const sourceById = id => state.sources.find(s => s.id === id) || null;
  const isDisk = id => id === 'array' || id === 'unassigned' || id === 'flash' || id.indexOf('pool:') === 0;
  const diskSourceName = id => id.indexOf('pool:') === 0 ? 'Pool: ' + id.slice(5) : ({ array: 'Array', unassigned: 'Unassigned disks', flash: 'Flash' }[id] || id);
  const sourceName = id => { const s = sourceById(id); return s ? (s.label || s.name) : (isDisk(id) ? diskSourceName(id) : 'Unavailable source'); };
  const groupById = id => draft.groups.find(g => g.id === id) || null;
  const pwmByKey = key => state.pwm.find(p => p.key === key) || null;
  const rpmByKey = key => state.rpm.find(r => r.key === key) || null;
  const rpmName = r => (r ? (r.label || r.driver_label || (r.chip + ' fan' + r.index)) : '');
  const rpmFullName = r => ((r.label || r.driver_label) ? rpmName(r) + ' (fan' + r.index + ')' : rpmName(r));
  const fanName = key => { const p = pwmByKey(key); return p ? (p.label || p.chip + ' PWM ' + p.index) : key; };

  function defaultBinding(source) {
    if (source === 'array' || source === 'unassigned') return { source, low: 35, high: 48, min_pwm: 170, max_pwm: 255, idle_pwm: 170 };
    if (isDisk(source)) return { source, low: 45, high: 65, min_pwm: 90, max_pwm: 255, idle_pwm: 90 }; // SSD/NVMe pools, flash
    if (source.indexOf('nvidia:') === 0) return { source, low: 45, high: 75, min_pwm: 90, max_pwm: 255 };
    return { source, low: 40, high: 70, min_pwm: 90, max_pwm: 255 };
  }

  function curvePwm(temp, b) {
    if (temp <= b.low) return b.min_pwm;
    if (temp >= b.high) return b.max_pwm;
    return Math.round(b.min_pwm + (temp - b.low) * (b.max_pwm - b.min_pwm) / (b.high - b.low));
  }

  /** Speed a binding asks for right now, mirrors pfc_binding_demand() in PHP. */
  function bindingDemand(b) {
    const s = sourceById(b.source);
    if (!s || s.state === 'error') return 255;
    if (s.state === 'parity') return b.max_pwm;
    if (s.state === 'idle') return b.idle_pwm != null ? b.idle_pwm : b.min_pwm;
    if (s.state === 'waiting') return Math.max(b.min_pwm, b.idle_pwm != null ? b.idle_pwm : b.min_pwm);
    return curvePwm(s.temp, b);
  }

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------- load */

  function load(withHistory) {
    const params = { action: 'state' };
    if (withHistory) params.history = 1;
    return $.getJSON(API, params).then(data => {
      state = data;
      if (data.history) history = data.history;
      // Only rebuild the editor when the saved config actually changed, so focus isn't lost
      if (!dirty && JSON.stringify(data.config) !== JSON.stringify(draft)) { draft = clone(data.config); groupsBuilt = false; }
      render();
    }).always(schedule);
  }

  function schedule() {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    const testing = state && state.fantest && state.fantest.phase !== 'done';
    const interval = testing ? 1000 : Math.max(2000, Math.min(5000, ((state && state.config.interval) || 5) * 1000));
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
      historyTick = (historyTick + 1) % 15;
      load(historyTick === 0);
    }, interval);
  }

  function markDirty() {
    dirty = true;
    $('#pfc-applybar').removeClass('pfc-hidden');
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ render */

  function render() {
    $('#pfc-applybar').toggleClass('pfc-hidden', !dirty);
    renderBanners();
    renderStatus();
    if (!groupsBuilt) buildGroups();
    updateGroups();
    renderPwmTable();
    renderRpmTable();
    renderFanTest();
    renderSources();
    renderDisks();
    renderHardware();
    fillCfgInputs();
  }

  function renderBanners() {
    const items = [];
    if (state.old_plugin) items.push(['warn', 'The old "Array Fan Control" plugin is still installed. Remove it under Plugins before enabling PWM Fan Control, otherwise both plugins will fight over the fans.']);
    if (state.migrated) items.push(['info', 'Your settings from "Array Fan Control" were imported as the group "Array fans". Check them, then enable fan control.']);
    state.errors.forEach(e => items.push(['error', e]));
    (state.status && state.status.warnings || []).forEach(w => items.push(['error', w]));
    if (state.config.enabled && !state.running) items.push(['error', 'Fan control is enabled but the service is not running. The watchdog will try to restart it within a minute. Check the syslog.']);
    const hw = state.hardware;
    if (!hw.writable) items.push(['error', 'No controllable fan outputs found. ' + (hw.hint || '') + ' See the hardware check at the bottom of this page.']);
    // Fans in a group that the service can't watch: no RPM sensor means no stall or moved-fan warnings
    const grouped = new Set(state.config.groups.flatMap(g => g.fans));
    const blind = state.pwm.filter(p => grouped.has(p.key) && !p.rpm_confirmed).map(p => p.label || p.key);
    if (blind.length) items.push(['info', 'Without a confirmed RPM sensor, the plugin can\'t tell if these fans stop or were moved to another header: ' +
      blind.join(', ') + '. Run Identify on them, or pick the sensor in the RPM sensor column ("none" if the fan has no sensor).']);
    $('#pfc-banners').html(items.map(i => '<div class="pfc-banner pfc-banner-' + i[0] + '">' + esc(i[1]) + '</div>').join(''));
  }

  function renderHardware() {
    const hw = state.hardware;
    const yes = t => '<span class="pfc-ok-text"><i class="fa fa-check"></i> ' + esc(t) + '</span>';
    const no = t => '<span class="pfc-error-text"><i class="fa fa-times"></i> ' + esc(t) + '</span>';
    const needLax = hw.conflicts.length && !hw.writable;
    const muted = t => '<span class="pfc-muted">' + esc(t) + '</span>';
    const rows = [
      ['Fan controller driver', hw.drivers.length ? yes(hw.drivers.join(', ')) : no('none loaded')],
      ['Fan outputs', hw.writable ? yes(hw.writable + ' found') : no(hw.pwm ? hw.pwm + ' found, none writable' : 'none found')],
      ['ACPI resource conflicts in the kernel log', hw.conflicts.length
        ? (needLax ? no('found') : muted(hw.lax ? 'found, handled by the lax option' : 'found, but fan outputs work')) +
          '<div class="pfc-log">' + esc(hw.conflicts.join('\n')) + '</div>'
        : yes('none')],
      ['acpi_enforce_resources=lax', hw.lax ? yes('set') : (needLax ? no('not set, needed') : muted('not set, not needed'))],
    ];
    if (hw.hint) rows.push(['What to do', esc(hw.hint)]);
    $('#pfc-hw-table tbody').html(rows.map(r => '<tr><td>' + esc(r[0]) + '</td><td>' + r[1] + '</td></tr>').join(''));
  }

  function renderStatus() {
    const st = state.status;
    const live = state.running && st;
    let html = '<div class="pfc-stat"><span class="pfc-stat-label">Service</span><span class="pfc-stat-value">' +
      (state.running ? 'Running' : (state.config.enabled ? 'Not running' : 'Disabled')) + '</span>' +
      '<span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + (live ? 'Checks every ' + st.interval + 's · updated ' + ago(st.time) : 'Showing a preview, fans are not changed') + '</span></div>';

    state.config.groups.forEach((g, i) => {
      const s = live && st.groups[g.id];
      const p = state.preview[g.id];
      const pwm = s ? s.pwm : (p ? p.pwm : null);
      const reason = s ? s.reason : (p ? p.reason : '');
      let note = '';
      if (s && s.slow_down_in != null) note = 'Slowing down to ' + pct(s.demand) + '% in ' + s.slow_down_in + 's';
      html += '<div class="pfc-stat" style="border-top:3px solid ' + COLORS[i % COLORS.length] + '">' +
        '<span class="pfc-stat-label">' + esc(g.name) + ' · ' + g.fans.length + ' fan' + (g.fans.length === 1 ? '' : 's') + '</span>' +
        '<span class="pfc-stat-value">' + (pwm == null ? '-' : pct(pwm) + '%' + (live ? '' : ' <span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">(preview)</span>')) + '</span>' +
        '<span class="pfc-small">' + esc(reason) + '</span>' +
        (note ? '<span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(note) + '</span>' : '') + '</div>';
    });
    if (!state.config.groups.length) html += '<div class="pfc-stat"><span class="pfc-stat-label">Groups</span><span class="pfc-small">No fan groups yet. Add one below.</span></div>';
    $('#pfc-status').html(html);
  }

  /* -------------------------------------------------------- group editor */

  function sourceOptions(group) {
    const used = new Set(group.sources.map(b => b.source));
    const opt = s => '<option value="' + esc(s.id) + '">' + esc((s.label || s.name) + (s.temp != null ? ' (' + fmtTemp(s.temp) + ')' : '')) + '</option>';
    const avail = state.sources.filter(s => !used.has(s.id));
    const sections = [
      ['Disks', avail.filter(s => s.type === 'disk')],
      ['GPUs', avail.filter(s => s.type === 'nvidia')],
      ['Sensors', avail.filter(s => s.type === 'hwmon')],
    ];
    return '<option value="">+ Add temperature source...</option>' +
      sections.filter(x => x[1].length).map(x => '<optgroup label="' + x[0] + '">' + x[1].map(opt).join('') + '</optgroup>').join('');
  }

  function buildGroups() {
    groupsBuilt = true;
    const owner = {};
    draft.groups.forEach(g => g.fans.forEach(f => { owner[f] = g; }));

    const html = draft.groups.map((g, gi) => {
      // Only named outputs are offered (plus the group's own fans), unnamed ones are usually empty headers
      const unnamed = state.pwm.filter(p => !p.label && g.fans.indexOf(p.key) < 0).map(p => p.key);
      const fanKeys = state.pwm.map(p => p.key).filter(k => showUnnamed || unnamed.indexOf(k) < 0);
      g.fans.forEach(k => { if (fanKeys.indexOf(k) < 0) fanKeys.push(k); }); // missing fans stay visible
      let fans = fanKeys.map(k => {
        const other = owner[k] && owner[k] !== g ? owner[k] : null;
        const p = pwmByKey(k);
        return '<label class="pfc-chip' + (g.fans.indexOf(k) >= 0 ? ' pfc-chip-on' : '') + (other ? ' pfc-chip-off' : '') + '"' +
          (other ? ' title="Already in ' + esc(other.name) + '"' : '') + '>' +
          '<input type="checkbox" class="pfc-g-fan" value="' + esc(k) + '"' + (g.fans.indexOf(k) >= 0 ? ' checked' : '') + (other ? ' disabled' : '') + '> ' +
          esc(fanName(k)) + (p ? '' : ' <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle" title="Not found"></i>') +
          (other ? ' <span class="pfc-muted">(' + esc(other.name) + ')</span>' : '') + '</label>';
      }).join('');
      if (!fans && unnamed.length) fans = '<span class="pfc-muted">No named fans yet. Name your fans in the Fans section below, then pick them here.</span>';
      if (unnamed.length) {
        fans += '<a href="#" class="pfc-toggle-unnamed pfc-small">' + (showUnnamed ? 'Hide unnamed outputs' :
          'Show ' + unnamed.length + ' unnamed output' + (unnamed.length === 1 ? '' : 's')) + '</a>';
      }

      const hasArray = g.sources.some(b => isDisk(b.source));
      const rows = g.sources.map((b, bi) => {
        const isArray = isDisk(b.source);
        const num = (field, val, min, max, unit) => '<input type="number" class="pfc-b-field pfc-narrow" data-b="' + bi + '" data-field="' + field + '" min="' + min + '" max="' + max + '" value="' + val + '">' + (unit || '');
        return '<tr data-b="' + bi + '">' +
          '<td><span class="pfc-swatch" style="background:' + COLORS[bi % COLORS.length] + '"></span>' + esc(sourceName(b.source)) + '</td>' +
          '<td>' + num('low', b.low, 0, 120) + '</td>' +
          '<td>' + num('high', b.high, 0, 120) + '</td>' +
          '<td>' + num('min_pwm', pct(b.min_pwm), 0, 100, '%') + '</td>' +
          '<td>' + num('max_pwm', pct(b.max_pwm), 0, 100, '%') + '</td>' +
          (hasArray ? '<td>' + (isArray ? num('idle_pwm', pct(b.idle_pwm), 0, 100, '%') : '<span class="pfc-muted">-</span>') + '</td>' : '') +
          '<td class="pfc-b-temp"></td><td class="pfc-b-wants"></td>' +
          '<td><button type="button" class="pfc-b-remove pfc-icon-btn" data-b="' + bi + '" title="Remove source"><i class="fa fa-times"></i></button></td></tr>';
      }).join('');

      return '<div class="pfc-group" data-g="' + gi + '">' +
        '<div class="pfc-group-head">' +
          '<span class="pfc-swatch pfc-swatch-lg" style="background:' + COLORS[gi % COLORS.length] + '"></span>' +
          '<input type="text" class="pfc-g-name" maxlength="40" value="' + esc(g.name) + '" placeholder="Group name">' +
          '<label class="pfc-muted">Slow-down delay <input type="number" class="pfc-g-ramp pfc-narrow" min="0" max="600" value="' + g.ramp_down + '"> s</label>' +
          '<span class="pfc-g-now"></span>' +
          '<button type="button" class="pfc-g-delete"><i class="fa fa-trash"></i> Delete group</button>' +
        '</div>' +
        '<div class="pfc-group-section"><div class="pfc-group-label">Fans</div><div class="pfc-chips">' + (fans || '<span class="pfc-muted">No fan outputs found.</span>') + '</div></div>' +
        '<div class="pfc-group-section"><div class="pfc-group-label">Temperature sources</div>' +
          '<div class="pfc-table-wrap"><table class="pfc-table pfc-bind-table"><thead><tr>' +
          '<th>Source</th><th>Low °C</th><th>High °C</th><th>Min speed</th><th>Max speed</th>' + (hasArray ? '<th>All disks spun down</th>' : '') + '<th>Now</th><th>Wants</th><th></th>' +
          '</tr></thead><tbody>' + (rows || '<tr><td colspan="9" class="pfc-muted">No sources yet. Add one below.</td></tr>') + '</tbody></table></div>' +
          '<select class="pfc-g-addsrc">' + sourceOptions(g) + '</select>' +
          '<p class="pfc-muted pfc-small">Below <b>Low</b> a source asks for the minimum speed, above <b>High</b> for the maximum speed, and in between for a speed on a straight line.</p>' +
          '<p class="pfc-g-hint pfc-warn-text pfc-small"></p>' +
        '</div>' +
        '<div class="pfc-charts">' +
          '<div class="pfc-chart-box"><div class="pfc-chart-title">Fan curves</div><svg class="pfc-chart pfc-curve" viewBox="0 0 560 260"></svg></div>' +
          '<div class="pfc-chart-box"><div class="pfc-chart-title">Last 24 hours <span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">(since reboot)</span></div><svg class="pfc-chart pfc-history" viewBox="0 0 560 260"></svg>' +
          '<div class="pfc-legend"><span class="pfc-key pfc-key-fan"></span>Fan speed (%) <span class="pfc-muted">· coloured lines: source temperatures (°C)</span></div></div>' +
        '</div></div>';
    }).join('');
    $('#pfc-groups').html(html || '<p class="pfc-muted">No fan groups yet.</p>');
  }

  /** Updates live values in the group editor without rebuilding it (keeps focus while typing). */
  function updateGroups() {
    const st = state.running && state.status;
    draft.groups.forEach((g, gi) => {
      const $g = $('#pfc-groups .pfc-group').filter(function () { return +this.dataset.g === gi; });
      g.sources.forEach((b, bi) => {
        const s = sourceById(b.source);
        const $tr = $g.find('.pfc-bind-table tr').filter(function () { return this.dataset.b === String(bi); });
        let temp = s ? fmtTemp(s.temp) : 'n/a';
        if (s && s.state !== 'ok') temp += ' <span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(s.detail) + '</span>';
        if (!s) temp = '<span class="pfc-error-text">not available</span>';
        $tr.find('.pfc-b-temp').html(temp);
        $tr.find('.pfc-b-wants').text(pct(bindingDemand(b)) + '%');
      });
      const live = st && st.groups[g.id];
      $g.find('.pfc-g-now').html(live ? 'Now <b>' + live.percent + '%</b>' : '');

      // Fans that may not start again at the lowest speed of this group (from their speed test)
      const lowest = Math.min(...g.sources.map(b => Math.min(b.min_pwm, b.idle_pwm != null ? b.idle_pwm : 255)));
      const hints = g.fans.map(pwmByKey).filter(p => { const from = fanSpinsFrom(p); return from != null && lowest > 0 && lowest < from; })
        .map(p => '"' + (p.label || fanName(p.key)) + '" needs ' + pct(fanSpinsFrom(p)) + '% to start');
      $g.find('.pfc-g-hint').html(hints.length ? '<i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i> The lowest speed in this group is ' + pct(lowest) +
        '%, but ' + esc(hints.join(', ')) + ' (speed test). Below that the fan may stop and not start again until the speed goes up. Set 0% if you want it to stop.' : '');
      drawCurve($g.find('.pfc-curve')[0], g);
      drawHistory($g.find('.pfc-history')[0], g);
    });
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- charts */

  const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const W = 560, H = 260, PAD = { l: 44, r: 14, t: 12, b: 30 };

  function svgEl(tag, attrs, text) {
    const el = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);
    Object.keys(attrs).forEach(k => el.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]));
    if (text != null) el.textContent = text;
    return el;
  }

  function axes(svg, x0, x1, y0, y1, xTicks, yTicks, xFmt, yFmt) {
    svg.innerHTML = '';
    const sx = v => PAD.l + (v - x0) * (W - PAD.l - PAD.r) / ((x1 - x0) || 1);
    const sy = v => H - PAD.b - (v - y0) * (H - PAD.t - PAD.b) / ((y1 - y0) || 1);
    yTicks.forEach(v => {
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('line', { x1: PAD.l, x2: W - PAD.r, y1: sy(v), y2: sy(v), class: 'pfc-grid' }));
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('text', { x: PAD.l - 6, y: sy(v) + 4, 'text-anchor': 'end', class: 'pfc-axis' }, yFmt(v)));
    });
    xTicks.forEach(v => {
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('line', { x1: sx(v), x2: sx(v), y1: PAD.t, y2: H - PAD.b, class: 'pfc-grid' }));
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('text', { x: sx(v), y: H - PAD.b + 18, 'text-anchor': 'middle', class: 'pfc-axis' }, xFmt(v)));
    });
    return { sx, sy };
  }

  function pathD(points, sx, sy) {
    let d = '', pen = false;
    points.forEach(p => {
      if (p[1] == null) { pen = false; return; }
      d += (pen ? 'L' : 'M') + sx(p[0]).toFixed(1) + ',' + sy(p[1]).toFixed(1);
      pen = true;
    });
    return d;
  }

  function drawCurve(svg, g) {
    if (!svg) return;
    const valid = g.sources.filter(b => b.low < b.high);
    if (!valid.length) {
      axes(svg, 0, 1, 0, 100, [], [0, 25, 50, 75, 100], v => v, v => v + '%');
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('text', { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, 'text-anchor': 'middle', class: 'pfc-axis' }, 'Add a temperature source to see its curve'));
      return;
    }
    const lo = Math.min(...valid.map(b => b.low)), hi = Math.max(...valid.map(b => b.high));
    const x0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((lo - 8) / 5) * 5), x1 = Math.ceil((hi + 8) / 5) * 5;
    const step = x1 - x0 > 60 ? 10 : 5;
    const xt = []; for (let t = x0; t <= x1; t += step) xt.push(t);
    const { sx, sy } = axes(svg, x0, x1, 0, 100, xt, [0, 25, 50, 75, 100], v => v + '°', v => v + '%');

    g.sources.forEach((b, bi) => {
      if (!(b.low < b.high)) return;
      const color = COLORS[bi % COLORS.length];
      const pts = [];
      for (let t = x0; t <= x1; t += 0.5) pts.push([t, pct(curvePwm(t, b))]);
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('path', { d: pathD(pts, sx, sy), class: 'pfc-line', stroke: color }));
      const s = sourceById(b.source);
      if (s && s.temp != null && s.state === 'ok') {
        const t = Math.max(x0, Math.min(x1, s.temp));
        const dot = svgEl('circle', { cx: sx(t), cy: sy(pct(curvePwm(s.temp, b))), r: 5, class: 'pfc-now', fill: color });
        dot.appendChild(svgEl('title', {}, sourceName(b.source) + ': ' + fmtTemp(s.temp) + ' → ' + pct(curvePwm(s.temp, b)) + '%'));
        svg.appendChild(dot);
      }
    });
  }

  function drawHistory(svg, g) {
    if (!svg) return;
    const rows = history.filter(h => h.g && h.g[g.id] != null);
    if (rows.length < 2) {
      axes(svg, 0, 1, 0, 100, [], [0, 25, 50, 75, 100], v => v, v => v);
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('text', { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, 'text-anchor': 'middle', class: 'pfc-axis' }, 'No history yet. Enable fan control and check back later.'));
      return;
    }
    const t0 = rows[0].t, t1 = rows[rows.length - 1].t, span = t1 - t0;
    const step = span > 43200 ? 3 * 3600 : span > 10800 ? 3600 : span > 3600 ? 1800 : 600;
    const xt = []; for (let t = Math.ceil(t0 / step) * step; t <= t1; t += step) xt.push(t);
    const fmt = t => { const d = new Date(t * 1000); return ('0' + d.getHours()).slice(-2) + ':' + ('0' + d.getMinutes()).slice(-2); };
    const temps = [];
    rows.forEach(h => g.sources.forEach(b => { const v = h.s && h.s[b.source]; if (v != null) temps.push(v); }));
    const yMax = Math.max(100, Math.ceil(Math.max(0, ...temps) / 25) * 25);
    const yt = []; for (let v = 0; v <= yMax; v += 25) yt.push(v);
    const { sx, sy } = axes(svg, t0, t1, 0, yMax, xt, yt, fmt, v => v);

    const series = get => {
      const out = [];
      rows.forEach((h, i) => {
        if (i && h.t - rows[i - 1].t > 180) out.push([h.t, null]); // gap: service was stopped
        out.push([h.t, get(h)]);
      });
      return out;
    };
    g.sources.forEach((b, bi) => {
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('path', { d: pathD(series(h => (h.s && h.s[b.source] != null ? h.s[b.source] : null)), sx, sy), class: 'pfc-line pfc-line-thin', stroke: COLORS[bi % COLORS.length] }));
    });
    svg.appendChild(svgEl('path', { d: pathD(series(h => pct(h.g[g.id])), sx, sy), class: 'pfc-line pfc-line-fan' }));
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------- fan table */

  function rpmOptions(p) {
    const prefix = p.key.slice(0, p.key.lastIndexOf('/') + 1);
    let html = '<option value="">Auto' + (p.guess_rpm ? ' (fan' + p.guess_rpm.split('/fan')[1] + ')' : '') + '</option><option value="none">None</option>';
    state.rpm.filter(r => r.key.indexOf(prefix) === 0).forEach(r => { html += '<option value="' + esc(r.key) + '">' + esc(rpmFullName(r)) + '</option>'; });
    return html;
  }

  /** Short text for a speed test result, e.g. "Stops below 20%, starts at 30%". */
  function testSummary(t) {
    if (!t || !t.done) return '';
    if (t.start_pwm == null) return 'Never stops, ' + t.max_rpm + ' RPM max';
    return 'Stops below ' + pct(t.min_pwm) + '%, starts at ' + pct(t.start_pwm) + '%';
  }

  /** Lowest speed at which a fan reliably runs, from its speed test (null without a test). */
  const fanSpinsFrom = p => (p && p.test && p.test.done ? (p.test.start_pwm != null ? p.test.start_pwm : p.test.min_pwm) : null);

  function renderPwmTable() {
    const $tb = $('#pfc-pwm-table tbody');
    if (!state.pwm.length) { $tb.html('<tr><td colspan="7" class="pfc-muted">No controllable fan outputs found.</td></tr>'); pwmSig = ''; return; }
    const sig = state.pwm.map(p => p.key).join('|') + '#' + state.rpm.map(r => r.key + '=' + r.label).join('|');
    if (sig !== pwmSig) {
      pwmSig = sig;
      $tb.html(state.pwm.map(p =>
        '<tr data-key="' + esc(p.key) + '">' +
        '<td><input type="text" class="pfc-label" maxlength="40" placeholder="e.g. GPU intake"></td>' +
        '<td><span class="pfc-output"></span><br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small pfc-path"></span></td>' +
        '<td class="pfc-speed"></td><td class="pfc-setting"></td>' +
        '<td><select class="pfc-rpm">' + rpmOptions(p) + '</select></td>' +
        '<td class="pfc-group-cell"></td>' +
        '<td class="pfc-nowrap"><button type="button" class="pfc-test-btn" data-mode="identify" title="Slow the fan down, then run it at full speed">Identify</button>' +
        '<button type="button" class="pfc-test-btn" data-mode="speed" title="Measure the RPM from 100% down to 0%: where the fan stops and where it starts again">Speed test</button></td></tr>').join(''));
    }
    const owner = {};
    draft.groups.forEach(g => g.fans.forEach(f => { owner[f] = g.name; }));
    const testing = state.fantest && state.fantest.phase !== 'done' ? state.fantest.key : null;

    state.pwm.forEach(p => {
      const $tr = $tb.find('tr').filter(function () { return this.dataset.key === p.key; });
      const label = $tr.find('.pfc-label')[0];
      if (!focused(label) && !label.dataset.dirty) label.value = p.label;
      $tr.find('.pfc-output').text(p.chip + ' · PWM ' + p.index);
      $tr.find('.pfc-path').text(p.hwmon + '/pwm' + p.index);
      const rpmTxt = p.rpm_key === 'none' ? '-' : (p.rpm == null ? 'n/a' : p.rpm + ' RPM');
      const guess = p.rpm_key && p.rpm_key !== 'none' && !p.rpm_confirmed;
      const summary = testSummary(p.test);
      $tr.find('.pfc-speed').html(esc(rpmTxt) +
        (guess ? ' <span class="pfc-muted pfc-small" title="Not confirmed yet. Use Identify to confirm.">(guess)</span>' : '') +
        (summary ? '<br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small" title="Result of the last speed test">' + esc(summary) + '</span>' : ''));
      $tr.find('.pfc-setting').html(p.value == null ? 'n/a' : esc(pct(p.value) + '% (' + p.value + ')') + '<br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(p.enable_name) +
        (p.mode === 0 ? ' · <span class="pfc-error-text" title="This header is in DC mode. Set it to PWM in the BIOS.">DC mode</span>' : '') + '</span>');
      const sel = $tr.find('.pfc-rpm')[0];
      if (!focused(sel)) sel.value = p.rpm_confirmed ? p.rpm_key : '';
      $tr.find('.pfc-group-cell').html(owner[p.key] ? esc(owner[p.key]) : '<span class="pfc-muted">-</span>');
      $tr.toggleClass('pfc-active-row', testing === p.key);
      $tr.find('.pfc-test-btn').prop('disabled', !!testing || !p.writable);
    });
  }

  function renderRpmTable() {
    const used = new Set(state.pwm.map(p => p.rpm_key).filter(Boolean));
    const others = state.rpm.filter(r => !used.has(r.key));
    $('#pfc-rpm-section').toggleClass('pfc-hidden', !others.length);
    const $tb = $('#pfc-rpm-table tbody');
    const sig = others.map(r => r.key).join('|');
    if (sig !== rpmSig) {
      rpmSig = sig;
      $tb.html(others.map(r =>
        '<tr data-key="' + esc(r.key) + '"><td><input type="text" class="pfc-rpm-label" maxlength="40" placeholder="e.g. Pump"></td>' +
        '<td>' + esc(r.chip + ' · fan' + r.index) + (r.driver_label ? '<br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(r.driver_label) + '</span>' : '') + '</td>' +
        '<td class="pfc-speed"></td></tr>').join(''));
    }
    others.forEach(r => {
      const $tr = $tb.find('tr').filter(function () { return this.dataset.key === r.key; });
      const input = $tr.find('.pfc-rpm-label')[0];
      if (!focused(input) && !input.dataset.dirty) input.value = r.label;
      $tr.find('.pfc-speed').text(r.rpm == null ? 'n/a' : r.rpm + ' RPM');
    });
  }

  /** The Identify / speed test panel below the fan table. */
  function renderFanTest() {
    const ft = state.fantest;
    const $box = $('#pfc-fantest');
    if (!ft || !ft.key || (ft.phase === 'done' && testDismissed === ft.time)) { $box.addClass('pfc-hidden'); return; }
    const running = ft.phase !== 'done';
    const speed = ft.mode === 'speed';
    const f = v => (v == null ? '-' : v);

    let html = '<div class="pfc-fantest-head"><b>' + (speed ? 'Speed test: ' : 'Identifying ') + esc(fanName(ft.key)) + '</b> ';
    if (running) {
      const step = ft.phase === 'starting' ? 'Starting' :
        ft.phase === 'low' ? 'Slowing down to ' + pct(ft.low_pwm || 0) + '%' :
        ft.phase === 'high' ? 'Full speed' :
        (ft.phase === 'up' ? 'Starting again at ' : 'Running at ') + pct(ft.pwm || 0) + '%';
      html += '<span class="pfc-muted">' + esc(step) + '...</span><button type="button" id="pfc-fantest-stop">Stop</button>';
    } else {
      html += '<button type="button" id="pfc-fantest-close">Close</button>';
    }
    html += '</div>';
    if (running) html += '<div class="pfc-progress"><div style="width:' + (ft.progress || 0) + '%"></div></div>';

    const samples = ft.samples || [];
    const current = samples.length ? samples[samples.length - 1].rpm : (ft.before || {});
    const keys = Object.keys(ft.before || current || {});
    if (keys.length) {
      // Identify: the last RPM of the slow and the full speed step. Speed test: at 100% and at the lowest
      // speed reached going down (the test stops going down once the fan stands still).
      const at = {};
      let lowest = 255;
      samples.forEach(s => {
        if (!speed) { at[s.phase] = s.rpm; return; }
        if (s.phase !== 'down') return;
        at[s.pwm] = s.rpm;
        lowest = Math.min(lowest, s.pwm);
      });
      const cols = speed ? [['100%', 255], [pct(lowest) + '%', lowest]] : [['Slow', 'low'], ['Full', 'high']];
      html += '<div class="pfc-fantest-body"><table class="pfc-table pfc-fantest-table"><thead><tr><th>RPM sensor</th><th>Before</th><th>Now</th>' +
        cols.map(c => '<th>' + c[0] + '</th>').join('') + '<th></th></tr></thead><tbody>';
      keys.forEach(k => {
        const r = rpmByKey(k);
        const reacted = (ft.reacted || []).indexOf(k) >= 0;
        html += '<tr class="' + (reacted ? 'pfc-reacted' : '') + '"><td>' + esc(r ? rpmFullName(r) : k) + '</td><td>' + f((ft.before || {})[k]) + '</td><td>' + f(current[k]) + '</td>' +
          cols.map(c => '<td>' + f((at[c[1]] || {})[k]) + '</td>').join('') +
          '<td>' + (reacted ? '<i class="fa fa-check"></i> reacted' : '') + '</td></tr>';
      });
      html += '</tbody></table>';
      if (speed && ft.result) html += '<div class="pfc-chart-box pfc-speed-chart"><svg class="pfc-chart" viewBox="0 0 560 260"></svg></div>';
      html += '</div>';
    } else {
      html += '<p class="pfc-muted">This chip has no RPM sensors, so watch or listen to the fans.</p>';
    }

    if (!running) {
      let result;
      const restored = ' The fan was restored to its previous setting.';
      if (ft.error === 'Stopped') result = 'Stopped.' + restored;
      else if (ft.error) result = ft.error + restored;
      else if (speed) result = 'Done. ' + testSummary(ft.result) + '. Keep the min speed of its group at or above the speed it starts at, so it always comes back after it stopped.' + restored;
      else if (ft.paired) result = 'Done. Paired with ' + rpmFullName(rpmByKey(ft.paired) || { label: ft.paired, index: '' }) + '.' + restored;
      else if ((ft.reacted || []).length > 1) result = 'Several sensors reacted. Pick the right one in the RPM sensor column.';
      else result = 'No RPM sensor reacted. Either nothing is connected, the fan has no RPM wire, or the header is set to DC instead of PWM in the BIOS. Did you see or hear a fan change speed?';
      html += '<p>' + esc(result) + '</p>';
    }
    $box.removeClass('pfc-hidden').html(html);
    if (speed && ft.result) drawSpeedTest($box.find('svg')[0], ft.result);
  }

  /** RPM at every speed step of a speed test. */
  function drawSpeedTest(svg, t) {
    const pts = t.points.filter(p => p[1] != null).map(p => [pct(p[0]), p[1]]).sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);
    const yMax = Math.max(500, Math.ceil(Math.max(...pts.map(p => p[1])) / 500) * 500);
    const yStep = yMax > 3000 ? 1000 : 500;
    const yt = []; for (let v = 0; v <= yMax; v += yStep) yt.push(v);
    const { sx, sy } = axes(svg, 0, 100, 0, yMax, [0, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100], yt, v => v + '%', v => v);
    if (t.start_pwm != null) {
      const x = sx(pct(t.start_pwm));
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('line', { x1: x, x2: x, y1: PAD.t, y2: H - PAD.b, class: 'pfc-marker' }));
      svg.appendChild(svgEl('text', { x: x + 4, y: PAD.t + 12, class: 'pfc-axis' }, 'starts at ' + pct(t.start_pwm) + '%'));
    }
    svg.appendChild(svgEl('path', { d: pathD(pts, sx, sy), class: 'pfc-line', stroke: COLORS[0] }));
    pts.forEach(p => {
      const dot = svgEl('circle', { cx: sx(p[0]), cy: sy(p[1]), r: 4, class: 'pfc-now', fill: COLORS[0] });
      dot.appendChild(svgEl('title', {}, p[0] + '%: ' + p[1] + ' RPM'));
      svg.appendChild(dot);
    });
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------ sources table */

  function renderSources() {
    const showAll = $('#pfc-show-all-sensors').prop('checked');
    const usedBy = {};
    draft.groups.forEach(g => g.sources.forEach(b => { (usedBy[b.source] = usedBy[b.source] || []).push(g.name); }));
    const list = state.sources.filter(s => showAll || s.type !== 'hwmon' || usedBy[s.id] || s.label);
    const hiddenCount = state.sources.length - list.length;

    const nv = state.nvidia;
    $('#pfc-nvidia-note').text(!nv.available ? 'No Nvidia driver found (nvidia-smi is missing), so no GPUs are listed.' : (nv.error ? 'Nvidia: ' + nv.error : ''));

    const $tb = $('#pfc-source-table tbody');
    const sig = list.map(s => s.id + '=' + s.label).join('|');
    if (sig !== sourceSig) {
      sourceSig = sig;
      const type = { disk: 'Disks', nvidia: 'Nvidia GPU', hwmon: 'Kernel sensor' };
      $tb.html(list.map(s =>
        '<tr data-key="' + esc(s.id) + '"><td><input type="text" class="pfc-source-label" maxlength="40" placeholder="' + esc(s.name) + '"></td>' +
        '<td>' + esc(s.name) + '<br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(type[s.type] || s.type) + '</span></td>' +
        '<td class="pfc-s-temp"></td><td class="pfc-s-used"></td></tr>').join('') +
        (hiddenCount ? '<tr><td colspan="4" class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + hiddenCount + ' more kernel sensor' + (hiddenCount === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' hidden.</td></tr>' : ''));
    }
    list.forEach(s => {
      const $tr = $tb.find('tr').filter(function () { return this.dataset.key === s.id; });
      const input = $tr.find('.pfc-source-label')[0];
      if (input && !focused(input) && !input.dataset.dirty) input.value = s.label;
      $tr.find('.pfc-s-temp').html(esc(fmtTemp(s.temp)) + (s.detail ? ' <span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(s.detail) + '</span>' : ''));
      $tr.find('.pfc-s-used').html(usedBy[s.id] ? esc(usedBy[s.id].join(', ')) : '<span class="pfc-muted">-</span>');
    });
  }

  function renderDisks() {
    const excluded = draft.array.exclude;
    const disks = state.disks.filter(d => d.device);
    const $tb = $('#pfc-disk-table tbody');
    if (!disks.length) { $tb.html('<tr><td colspan="5" class="pfc-muted">No disks found.</td></tr>'); return; }
    $tb.html(disks.map(d => {
      const usable = !!d.source;
      const use = usable && excluded.indexOf(d.name) < 0;
      const src = usable ? sourceById(d.source) : null;
      const hot = src && src.detail === 'hottest is ' + d.name;
      return '<tr class="' + (use ? '' : 'pfc-dim') + '">' +
        '<td><input type="checkbox" class="pfc-disk-use" data-name="' + esc(d.name) + '"' + (use ? ' checked' : '') + (usable ? '' : ' disabled title="' + esc(d.type) + ' disks are not used"') + '></td>' +
        '<td>' + esc(d.name) + (hot ? ' <i class="fa fa-fire pfc-hot" title="Hottest disk of ' + esc(sourceName(d.source)) + '"></i>' : '') + '<br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(d.device) + '</span></td>' +
        '<td>' + (usable ? esc(sourceName(d.source)) : '<span class="pfc-muted">-</span>') + '<br><span class="pfc-muted pfc-small">' + esc(d.type) + '</span></td><td>' + (d.spundown ? 'Standby' : 'Active') + '</td>' +
        '<td>' + (d.spundown ? 'Spun down' : esc(fmtTemp(d.temp))) + '</td></tr>';
    }).join(''));
  }

  function fillCfgInputs() {
    $('[data-cfg]', root).each(function () {
      if (focused(this)) return;
      const v = getPath(draft, this.dataset.cfg);
      if (this.type === 'checkbox') this.checked = !!v;
      else this.value = String(this.dataset.type === 'pct' ? pct(v) : v);
    });
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- events */

  const $groups = $('#pfc-groups');
  const gIndex = el => +$(el).closest('.pfc-group')[0].dataset.g;
  const rebuild = () => { buildGroups(); updateGroups(); renderPwmTable(); renderSources(); renderStatus(); };

  $('#pfc-add-group').on('click', () => {
    const id = 'g' + Math.random().toString(16).slice(2, 10);
    draft.groups.push({ id, name: draft.groups.length ? 'New group' : 'Array fans', fans: [], ramp_down: draft.groups.length ? 30 : 0, sources: [] });
    markDirty();
    rebuild();
  });

  $groups
    .on('input', '.pfc-g-name', function () { draft.groups[gIndex(this)].name = this.value; markDirty(); })
    .on('change', '.pfc-g-name', () => rebuild())
    .on('input', '.pfc-g-ramp', function () { draft.groups[gIndex(this)].ramp_down = parseInt(this.value, 10) || 0; markDirty(); })
    .on('change', '.pfc-g-fan', function () {
      const g = draft.groups[gIndex(this)];
      g.fans = g.fans.filter(k => k !== this.value);
      if (this.checked) g.fans.push(this.value);
      markDirty();
      rebuild();
    })
    .on('input', '.pfc-b-field', function () {
      const g = draft.groups[gIndex(this)];
      const b = g.sources[+this.dataset.b];
      const field = this.dataset.field;
      const v = parseFloat(this.value);
      if (isNaN(v)) return;
      b[field] = /_pwm$/.test(field) ? toPwm(v) : Math.round(v);
      markDirty();
      updateGroups();
    })
    .on('click', '.pfc-b-remove', function () {
      draft.groups[gIndex(this)].sources.splice(+this.dataset.b, 1);
      markDirty();
      rebuild();
    })
    .on('change', '.pfc-g-addsrc', function () {
      if (!this.value) return;
      draft.groups[gIndex(this)].sources.push(defaultBinding(this.value));
      markDirty();
      rebuild();
    })
    .on('click', '.pfc-g-delete', function () {
      const gi = gIndex(this);
      if (!confirm('Delete the group "' + draft.groups[gi].name + '"? Its fans go back to the BIOS after you click Apply.')) return;
      draft.groups.splice(gi, 1);
      markDirty();
      rebuild();
    });

  $(root).on('change input', '[data-cfg]', function () {
    let v = this.type === 'checkbox' ? this.checked : this.value;
    if (this.dataset.type === 'bool') v = v === 'true' || v === true;
    if (this.dataset.type === 'int') v = parseInt(v, 10) || 0;
    if (this.dataset.type === 'pct') v = toPwm(parseFloat(v) || 0);
    setPath(draft, this.dataset.cfg, v);
    markDirty();
    if (/^array\./.test(this.dataset.cfg)) renderDisks();
  });

  $('#pfc-disk-table').on('change', '.pfc-disk-use', function () {
    const list = draft.array.exclude.filter(n => n !== this.dataset.name);
    if (!this.checked) list.push(this.dataset.name);
    draft.array.exclude = list;
    markDirty();
    renderDisks();
  });

  $(root).on('click', '.pfc-apply', function () {
    $('.pfc-apply').prop('disabled', true);
    post({ action: 'save_config', config: JSON.stringify(draft) })
      .then(() => { dirty = false; return load(true); }, showError)
      .always(() => $('.pfc-apply').prop('disabled', false));
  });

  $(root).on('click', '.pfc-reset', () => {
    dirty = false;
    draft = clone(state.config);
    groupsBuilt = false;
    render();
  });

  // Names are saved right away (they don't change how fans are controlled)
  function labelSaver(selector, action, after) {
    $(root)
      .on('input', selector, function () { this.dataset.dirty = '1'; })
      .on('keydown', selector, function (e) { if (e.key === 'Enter') this.blur(); })
      .on('change', selector, function () {
        const el = this;
        post({ action, key: $(el).closest('tr')[0].dataset.key, label: el.value })
          .then(() => { delete el.dataset.dirty; return load(); }, showError)
          .then(() => { if (after) after(); });
      });
  }
  labelSaver('.pfc-label', 'save_fan', () => { buildGroups(); updateGroups(); });
  labelSaver('.pfc-rpm-label', 'save_rpm_label');
  labelSaver('.pfc-source-label', 'save_source_label', () => { buildGroups(); updateGroups(); });

  $('#pfc-pwm-table')
    .on('change', '.pfc-rpm', function () { post({ action: 'save_fan', key: $(this).closest('tr')[0].dataset.key, rpm: this.value }).then(() => load(), showError); })
    .on('click', '.pfc-test-btn', function () {
      const key = $(this).closest('tr')[0].dataset.key;
      const mode = this.dataset.mode;
      if (mode === 'speed' && !confirm('Speed test "' + fanName(key) + '"?\n\nThe fan is stepped from 100% down to 0% and back up, which takes about a minute. ' +
        'It stops for a while, so don\'t run this on a fan that is cooling something hot right now.')) return;
      testDismissed = null;
      post({ action: 'fantest', key, mode }).then(() => load(), showError);
    });

  $('#pfc-fantest')
    .on('click', '#pfc-fantest-stop', () => post({ action: 'fantest_stop' }).then(() => load(), showError))
    .on('click', '#pfc-fantest-close', () => { testDismissed = state.fantest.time; renderFanTest(); });

  $('#pfc-show-all-sensors').on('change', () => { sourceSig = ''; renderSources(); });
  $(root).on('click', '.pfc-toggle-unnamed', e => { e.preventDefault(); showUnnamed = !showUnnamed; buildGroups(); updateGroups(); });

  window.addEventListener('beforeunload', e => { if (dirty) { e.preventDefault(); e.returnValue = ''; } });

  load(true);
})(jQuery);
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/scripts/daemon.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - background service. Started and stopped by rc.pwmfancontrol.
 * The control loop itself is in include/controller.php.
 */
require_once dirname(__DIR__) . '/include/common.php';
require_once dirname(__DIR__) . '/include/controller.php';

@mkdir(PFC_RUN, 0777, true);
$lock = fopen(PFC_RUN . '/daemon.lock', 'c');
if (!$lock || !flock($lock, LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB)) {
    fwrite(STDERR, "PWM Fan Control is already running\n");
    exit(0);
}
file_put_contents(PFC_PIDFILE, (string)getmypid());

$controller = new PfcController();
$finished = false;

// A crash (fatal PHP error) must not leave the fans at a low speed: run them at full speed
// until the watchdog has restarted the service.
register_shutdown_function(function () use ($controller, &$finished) {
    if ($finished) return;
    $error = error_get_last();
    $msg = 'The service crashed, fans run at full speed until the watchdog restarts it (within a minute)' . ($error ? ': ' . $error['message'] : '.');
    pfc_log($msg);
    $controller->failsafe();
    pfc_notify_limited('service', 'Service crashed', $msg); // shares its hourly limit with the watchdog alert
});

if (function_exists('pcntl_async_signals')) {
    pcntl_async_signals(true);
    $stop = function () use ($controller) { $controller->running = false; };
    pcntl_signal(SIGTERM, $stop);
    pcntl_signal(SIGINT, $stop);
    pcntl_signal(SIGHUP, SIG_IGN);
}

$controller->run();
$finished = true;
if ((int)@file_get_contents(PFC_PIDFILE) === getmypid()) @unlink(PFC_PIDFILE);
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/scripts/fantest.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - tests a single PWM output, started from the web UI.
 * Usage: php fantest.php identify|speed <fan key>
 *
 *   identify  Slows the fan down until it stops slowing, then runs it at full speed, so you can see and
 *             hear which fan it is.
 *   speed     Steps the fan down from 100% and records the RPM at every step, until it stops (or 0% is
 *             reached). Then finds the speed it needs to start again, trying from the lowest speed it
 *             kept running at upwards. The fan stands still only for a few seconds at a time.
 *
 * Every RPM sensor on the same chip is sampled once per second. Progress is written to PFC_FANTEST so
 * the web UI can show it live. If exactly one sensor reacts, it is paired with the output.
 *
 * While a test runs, the service leaves this fan alone. So the test is stopped right away when the fan's
 * group needs it (a temperature reaches "high", can't be read, or a parity check starts), see
 * pfc_fan_needed(). The output is always restored to its previous speed and mode afterwards.
 */
require_once dirname(__DIR__) . '/include/common.php';

const PFC_SPEED_DOWN   = [255, 204, 153, 102, 77, 51, 38, 26, 13, 0]; // 100% .. 0%
const PFC_SPEED_UP     = [26, 38, 51, 77, 102, 153, 204, 255];        // start tries, from the lowest running speed up
const PFC_SPEED_STEP   = 5;   // seconds per step going down: time for the RPM to settle
const PFC_START_STEP   = 3;   // seconds per start try: a fan that starts does so within 1-2 seconds
const PFC_FOLLOW_PWM   = 102; // from this step on, sensors that follow the speed changes are watched for a stop
const PFC_NEEDED_EVERY = 2;   // seconds between checks whether the fan's group needs the fan
const PFC_SETTLE_MAX   = 30;  // Identify: longest wait for a fan to finish slowing down

$mode = $argv[1] ?? '';
$key = $argv[2] ?? '';
$cfg = pfc_load_config();
$hw = pfc_scan_hwmon();
if (!in_array($mode, ['identify', 'speed'], true) || !isset($hw['pwm'][$key])) {
    pfc_write_json(PFC_FANTEST, ['key' => $key, 'mode' => $mode, 'phase' => 'done', 'error' => 'Fan not found', 'time' => time()]);
    exit(1);
}

$fan = $hw['pwm'][$key];
$path = $fan['path'];
$chip_prefix = substr($key, 0, strrpos($key, '/') + 1);
$sensors = array_filter($hw['rpm'], fn($k) => strpos($k, $chip_prefix) === 0, ARRAY_FILTER_USE_KEY);
$fans = pfc_load_fans();
$paired = pfc_confirmed_rpm($fans, $key);

$low_pwm = max(0, min(255, (int)$cfg['identify']['low_pwm']));
$seconds = max(3, min(30, (int)$cfg['identify']['seconds']));
$total = $mode === 'identify' ? 2 * $seconds + 5 : count(PFC_SPEED_DOWN) * PFC_SPEED_STEP + 2;

$state = [
    'key'      => $key,
    'mode'     => $mode,
    'pid'      => getmypid(),
    'phase'    => $mode === 'identify' ? 'low' : 'down',
    'pwm'      => null,      // speed being tested right now
    'time'     => time(),
    'progress' => 0,         // percent, an estimate for the speed test
    'low_pwm'  => $low_pwm,
    'before'   => [],        // RPM of every sensor before the test
    'samples'  => [],        // [{phase, pwm, rpm: {sensor key: rpm}}], once per second
    'reacted'  => [],        // sensors that followed the speed changes
    'paired'   => null,      // sensor paired by this test
    'result'   => null,      // speed test result, also stored in fans.json
    'error'    => null,
];

// Always restore the fan, whatever happens
$orig_value = $fan['value'] ?? PFC_FAILSAFE_PWM;
$orig_enable = $fan['enable'];
$restored = false;
$restore = function () use ($path, $orig_value, $orig_enable, &$restored) {
    if ($restored) return;
    $restored = true;
    @file_put_contents($path, (string)$orig_value);
    if ($orig_enable !== null) @file_put_contents("{$path}_enable", (string)$orig_enable);
};
register_shutdown_function($restore);
if (function_exists('pcntl_async_signals')) {
    pcntl_async_signals(true);
    foreach ([SIGTERM, SIGINT, SIGHUP] as $sig) pcntl_signal($sig, function () { exit(1); });
}

$sample = function () use ($sensors): array {
    $out = [];
    foreach ($sensors as $k => $s) $out[$k] = pfc_read_int($s['path']);
    return $out;
};

$needed = null; // why the test was stopped because the fan was needed

/**
 * Runs the fan at $pwm for up to $secs seconds, sampling once per second. Ends early when $until($rpm)
 * returns true. Returns the last RPM sample, or null when the test was stopped (by the user, or because
 * the fan's group needs the fan).
 */
$hold = function (string $phase, int $pwm, int $secs, ?callable $until = null)
        use (&$state, &$total, &$needed, $path, $sample, $cfg, $key): ?array {
    $state['phase'] = $phase;
    $state['pwm'] = $pwm;
    @file_put_contents($path, (string)$pwm);
    $rpm = [];
    for ($i = 1; $i <= $secs; $i++) {
        sleep(1);
        $rpm = $sample();
        $state['samples'][] = ['phase' => $phase, 'pwm' => $pwm, 'rpm' => $rpm];
        $state['progress'] = max($state['progress'], min(99, (int)round(count($state['samples']) * 100 / max(1, $total))));
        pfc_write_json(PFC_FANTEST, $state);
        if (is_file(PFC_STOP_FLAG)) return null;
        if (count($state['samples']) % PFC_NEEDED_EVERY === 0 && ($needed = pfc_fan_needed($cfg, $key)) !== null) return null;
        if ($until && $until($rpm)) break;
    }
    return $rpm;
};

/** Sensors whose RPM at $high is clearly above their RPM at $low, best first. */
$reacting = function (array $low, array $high) use ($sensors): array {
    $scores = [];
    foreach ($sensors as $k => $_) {
        $l = (int)($low[$k] ?? 0);
        $h = (int)($high[$k] ?? 0);
        if ($h > 0 && $h * 10 > $l * 13 && $h - $l > 150) $scores[$k] = $h - $l;
    }
    arsort($scores);
    return array_keys($scores);
};

$state['before'] = $sample();
pfc_write_json(PFC_FANTEST, $state);
if ($orig_enable !== null && $orig_enable !== 1) @file_put_contents("{$path}_enable", '1');

$stopped = false;
if ($mode === 'identify') {
    // A fan takes longer to slow down than to speed up, so the slow step lasts until the RPM has
    // stopped falling (at least $seconds, at most PFC_SETTLE_MAX), and the change is easy to see.
    // Without a paired sensor: the sensors that dropped clearly since the start. Other fans on the chip
    // can be changing speed at the same time (their group), they must not keep the step going.
    $history = [];
    $settled = function (array $rpm) use (&$history, &$state, $paired, $sensors, $seconds): bool {
        $history[] = $rpm;
        $n = count($history);
        if ($n < $seconds || $n < 4) return false;
        $watch = $paired ? [$paired] : array_keys(array_filter($sensors, fn($s, $k) =>
            (int)($rpm[$k] ?? 0) < 0.85 * (int)($state['before'][$k] ?? 0), ARRAY_FILTER_USE_BOTH));
        foreach ($watch as $k) {
            $now = (int)($rpm[$k] ?? 0);
            $before = (int)($history[$n - 4][$k] ?? 0);
            if ($now < $before * 0.97) return false; // still slowing down
        }
        return true;
    };
    $low = $hold('low', $low_pwm, max($seconds, PFC_SETTLE_MAX), $settled);
    $total = count($state['samples']) + $seconds;
    $high = $low === null ? null : $hold('high', 255, $seconds);
    if ($high === null) $stopped = true;
    else $state['reacted'] = $reacting($low, $high);
} else {
    // Down: record the RPM at every step, and stop going down once the fan stands still. Which sensor
    // belongs to the fan is known once the speed has dropped a bit: the ones that follow the steps.
    $down = [];
    $watch = $paired ? [$paired] : [];
    $isStopped = function (array $rpm) use (&$watch): bool {
        foreach ($watch as $k) if (($rpm[$k] ?? null) === 0) return true;
        return false;
    };
    foreach (PFC_SPEED_DOWN as $pwm) {
        $check = $watch && $pwm !== 255 ? $isStopped : null; // at 100% a fan may still be spinning up from standstill
        $rpm = $hold('down', $pwm, PFC_SPEED_STEP + ($pwm === 255 ? 2 : 0), $check); // the first step may spin up from slow
        if ($rpm === null) { $stopped = true; break; }
        $down[$pwm] = $rpm;
        if ($check && $isStopped($rpm)) break;
        if (!$paired && $pwm === PFC_FOLLOW_PWM) {
            $watch = array_keys(array_filter($rpm, fn($r, $k) => $r !== null && (int)($down[255][$k] ?? 0) > 0 && $r < 0.8 * $down[255][$k], ARRAY_FILTER_USE_BOTH));
        }
    }
    if (!$stopped) {
        $last = array_key_last($down);
        $state['reacted'] = $reacting($down[$last], $down[255]);
        $sensor = $paired ?? (count($state['reacted']) === 1 ? $state['reacted'][0] : null);
        if ($sensor === null) {
            $state['error'] = count($state['reacted']) > 1
                ? 'Several RPM sensors reacted. Pick the right one in the RPM sensor column, then run the test again.'
                : 'No RPM sensor reacted, so the speeds could not be measured.';
        } else {
            $points = [];
            foreach ($down as $pwm => $rpm) $points[] = [$pwm, $rpm[$sensor] ?? null];
            $running = array_filter($points, fn($p) => (int)$p[1] > 0);
            $min_pwm = $running ? min(array_column($running, 0)) : null;
            $start_pwm = null;
            if ($min_pwm === null) $state['error'] = 'The fan did not spin at any speed. Check the fan, its cable and the RPM sensor pairing.';
            // Up: the fan stopped, find the speed it needs to start again. It can't start below the lowest
            // speed it kept running at, so the tries begin there.
            if ($min_pwm !== null && ($down[$last][$sensor] ?? null) === 0) {
                $tries = array_values(array_filter(PFC_SPEED_UP, fn($p) => $p >= $min_pwm));
                $total = count($state['samples']) + count($tries) * PFC_START_STEP;
                $started = fn($rpm) => (int)($rpm[$sensor] ?? 0) > 0;
                foreach ($tries as $pwm) {
                    $rpm = $hold('up', $pwm, PFC_START_STEP, $started);
                    if ($rpm === null) { $stopped = true; break; }
                    if ($started($rpm)) { $start_pwm = $pwm; break; }
                }
                if (!$stopped && $start_pwm === null) $state['error'] = 'The fan did not start again, not even at 100%. Check the fan.';
            }
            if (!$stopped && $min_pwm !== null && !$state['error']) {
                $state['result'] = [
                    'done' => true, 'time' => time(), 'rpm_key' => $sensor, 'points' => $points,
                    'max_rpm' => $down[255][$sensor] ?? null,
                    'min_pwm' => $min_pwm,        // lowest speed it keeps running at
                    'start_pwm' => $start_pwm,    // speed it needs to start from standstill (null: never stops)
                ];
            }
        }
    }
}
$restore();
@unlink(PFC_STOP_FLAG);

if ($stopped) {
    $state['error'] = $needed !== null ? "Stopped early, the fan is needed: $needed. Try again when it is cooler." : 'Stopped';
    if ($needed !== null) pfc_log("Fan test of $key stopped early, the fan is needed: $needed");
} else {
    // Store the pairing (when exactly one sensor reacted) and the speed test result
    $fans = pfc_load_fans();
    if (!$paired && count($state['reacted']) === 1) {
        $fans['pwm'][$key]['rpm'] = $state['paired'] = $state['reacted'][0];
    }
    if ($state['result']) $fans['pwm'][$key]['test'] = $state['result'];
    pfc_save_fans($fans);
}

$state['phase'] = 'done';
$state['progress'] = 100;
$state['time'] = time();
pfc_write_json(PFC_FANTEST, $state);
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/scripts/rc.pwmfancontrol">
<INLINE><![CDATA[#!/bin/bash
# PWM Fan Control service control
# Usage: rc.pwmfancontrol start|stop|restart|status|watchdog

NAME="pwm.fan.control"
PLUGIN="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$NAME"
PIDFILE="/var/run/$NAME.pid"
STATUS="/tmp/$NAME/status.json"
PHP=/usr/bin/php

running() {
    [[ -f "$PIDFILE" ]] && kill -0 "$(cat "$PIDFILE" 2>/dev/null)" 2>/dev/null
}

# Unraid alert notification (if enabled). At most one service alert an hour, shared with the crash alert
# of the service itself, so a service that keeps failing doesn't flood.
alert() {
    "$PHP" -r 'require $argv[1]; pfc_notify_limited("service", "Service restarted", $argv[2]);' "$PLUGIN/include/common.php" "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1
}

start() {
    if running; then
        echo "PWM Fan Control is already running"
        return 0
    fi
    setsid nohup "$PHP" "$PLUGIN/scripts/daemon.php" >/dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &
    for _ in $(seq 1 30); do
        running && { echo "PWM Fan Control started"; return 0; }
        sleep 0.1
    done
    echo "PWM Fan Control did not start (is it enabled?)"
    return 1
}

stop() {
    if running; then
        local pid
        pid=$(cat "$PIDFILE")
        kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null
        for _ in $(seq 1 50); do
            kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null || break
            sleep 0.1
        done
        kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null && kill -9 "$pid" 2>/dev/null
    fi
    rm -f "$PIDFILE"
    # Make sure every fan is handed back to the BIOS, even if the daemon was killed
    "$PHP" "$PLUGIN/scripts/release.php"
    echo "PWM Fan Control stopped"
}

case "$1" in
    start)    start ;;
    stop)     stop ;;
    restart)  stop; start ;;
    status)   if running; then echo "running (pid $(cat "$PIDFILE"))"; else echo "stopped"; exit 1; fi ;;
    watchdog)
        # Called by cron every minute while fan control is enabled
        if ! running; then
            logger -t "$NAME" "Service was not running, restarting it"
            alert "The fan control service was not running and has been restarted. Check the syslog for the reason."
            start >/dev/null
        else
            # The service writes its status on every check (at most every 30s). If it hasn't
            # for 90s it is stuck, e.g. on a hanging driver: restart it.
            now=$(date +%s)
            last=$(stat -c %Y "$STATUS" 2>/dev/null || stat -c %Y "$PIDFILE" 2>/dev/null || echo "$now")
            if (( now - last > 90 )); then
                logger -t "$NAME" "Service stopped responding, restarting it"
                alert "The fan control service stopped responding and has been restarted. Fans ran at their last speed in the meantime. Check the syslog for the reason."
                stop >/dev/null
                start >/dev/null
            fi
        fi
        ;;
    *) echo "Usage: $0 start|stop|restart|status|watchdog"; exit 1 ;;
esac
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/scripts/release.php">
<INLINE><![CDATA[<?php
/*
 * PWM Fan Control - hands every fan we have taken over back to the BIOS.
 * Called by "rc.pwmfancontrol stop", also when the daemon was killed without cleaning up.
 */
require_once dirname(__DIR__) . '/include/common.php';
pfc_release_all();
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- Install -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[#!/bin/bash
# Runs after the plugin files are written (on install, update and every boot)
NAME=pwm.fan.control
PLUGIN="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$NAME"
chmod +x "$PLUGIN/scripts/rc.pwmfancontrol"
mkdir -p "/boot/config/plugins/$NAME" "/tmp/$NAME"

# Stop a running copy from before an update, then start again if enabled
[[ -f "/var/run/$NAME.pid" ]] && "$PLUGIN/scripts/rc.pwmfancontrol" stop >/dev/null 2>&1
/usr/bin/php -r "require '$PLUGIN/include/common.php'; pfc_migrate_old(); pfc_apply_service(pfc_load_config());"

echo ""
echo "PWM Fan Control is installed."
echo "Open Settings > Utilities > PWM Fan Control to identify, name and group your fans."
echo ""
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- Remove -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE><![CDATA[#!/bin/bash
# Runs when the plugin is removed. Settings in /boot/config/plugins/pwm.fan.control are kept.
NAME=pwm.fan.control
PLUGIN="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$NAME"
[[ -x "$PLUGIN/scripts/rc.pwmfancontrol" ]] && "$PLUGIN/scripts/rc.pwmfancontrol" stop
rm -f "/boot/config/plugins/$NAME/$NAME.cron"
/usr/local/sbin/update_cron
rm -rf "$PLUGIN" "/tmp/$NAME" "/var/run/$NAME.pid"
echo "PWM Fan Control removed. Fans were handed back to the BIOS."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
